<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f6421a7b5e686f7cee3815260dfc1bf74d0be23e> <http://schema.org/description> "This report presents the findings of the first year of bird surveys undertaken at Kyle Rhea to inform the EIA of the proposed Kyle Rhea Tidal Array.\r\nAlthough marine mammal and basking shark were surveyed as part of the same programme of fieldwork, the results of for these species are reported separately (Year 1 Marine Mammal and Basking Shark Report). The survey work is on-going and it is planned to complete to two full years of baseline characterisation studies." .
_:eda953a26baf9e52f6c4a965879e11f9 <http://schema.org/value> "Kyle Rhea" .
_:a28533ca3440b73b79ba490123e99c42 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:eb98e22d5378e73aae4be4be72583d9 <http://schema.org/name> "marine species" .
_:bdb2da920bc74106ee3f932c556e9bbb <http://schema.org/value> "NEG Micon UK Ltd." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f639e2684d6b983351a43964b566dadc188da2aa> <http://schema.org/description> "In accordance with the FEPA licence, there is a requirement to undertake pre-construction and post-construction bathymetric surveys of a selection of turbine locations and the associated cable corridor to determine rates of scour around the turbines after construction. Emu Limited was commissioned by NEG Micon UK Ltd. to perform a series of hydrographic surveys of these areas in order to determine whether any souring occurs around the turbines or significant changes to the seabed profile have been made during construction of the windfarm. This project relates to the second post-construction swath survey which was carried out on 20th November 2005 from the vessel Emu surveyor." .
_:bdb2da920bc74106ee3f932c556e9bbb <http://schema.org/value> "Emu Limited" .
_:bdb2da920bc74106ee3f932c556e9bbb <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
