_:e1bd6810bdacfd79415cae46d71263ac <http://schema.org/value> "London Array" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f3933e7c012a5e6a31e029262505a791bd021604> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e1bd6810bdacfd79415cae46d71263ac .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f3933e7c012a5e6a31e029262505a791bd021604> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f3933e7c012a5e6a31e029262505a791bd021604> <http://schema.org/description> "This document is a report on the second year (2014) of post-installation archaeological\r\nmonitoring of geophysical survey data which was acquired during the autumn of 2014 for the\r\nturbine array and export cables following the construction of the wind farm. This data was\r\nreviewed by the London Array Retained Archaeologists in order to ascertain if post-installation\r\nsediment dynamics had had any effect on the Archaeological Avoidance Blocks (AABs) identified\r\nand agreed during the consent and construction process, or whether any further potential\r\narchaeological material had been exposed by bed movement caused by the wind farm\r\ninstallation." .
_:e1bd6810bdacfd79415cae46d71263ac <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e1bd6810bdacfd79415cae46d71263ac <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f3837a26d7f27df0587623953e81b759ac14e374> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f3837a26d7f27df0587623953e81b759ac14e374> <http://schema.org/description> "The Joint Cetacean Data Programme (JCDP) aims to promote and facilitate streamlined access to cetacean survey data collected from vessel and aerial platforms, by collating the growing evidence-base across the northeast Atlantic into a single accessible resource.\r\n The JCDP encourages data collectors to come together to make high quality standardised data more readily available via the JCDP Data Portal and enable development of open access data products to better inform research. The project has produced an agreed Data Standard and created a dedicated online portal to host cetacean survey data collected from vessel and aerial platforms, as well as a number of key data products that will be developed from the data.\r\n More information about the programme is available on the JCDP Information Portal: www.jncc.gov.uk/JCDP" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f3837a26d7f27df0587623953e81b759ac14e374> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f5c4ae444a76b8dde67710815b10f4c2 .
