<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f195abb9ba141af6d55954a3aae335d3eb33b0c6> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e3a169a933d399fd5540a3d9f6cae514 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f195abb9ba141af6d55954a3aae335d3eb33b0c6> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:decb6c254aa2cfeb9da7556e1a031b7e .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f195abb9ba141af6d55954a3aae335d3eb33b0c6> <http://schema.org/description> "Two rocky-shore sites on the Isle of Cumbrae, Farland Point and White Bay, are surveyed semi-annually (March/April and August/September) in class exercises in undergraduate marine biology field courses. White Bay (a relatively sheltered shore) is located at the northern end of the island, while Farland Point (a moderately exposed shore) is located towards the south. Farland Point is subjected to prevailing SW winds. At both sites, the shore profile is measured and the abundance of selected species is assessed semi-quantitatively on an ESACFOR scale. The presence of other species is recorded in relation to major littoral zone (littoral fringe, eulittoral zone, sublittoral fringe) and microhabitat (on algae; in kelp holdfasts; under overhangs or in crevices; in rockpools; on open rock; under stones)." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f188b5a93f8c8d7b4c5e672546b09a298c5bffba> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fdc30a4d70655050550e41429f2f1bd3 .
_:fdc30a4d70655050550e41429f2f1bd3 <http://schema.org/value> "Rudall Blanchard Associates" .
_:fdc30a4d70655050550e41429f2f1bd3 <http://schema.org/value> "Eclipse Energy Company Ltd" .
_:fdc30a4d70655050550e41429f2f1bd3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f188b5a93f8c8d7b4c5e672546b09a298c5bffba> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f188b5a93f8c8d7b4c5e672546b09a298c5bffba> <http://schema.org/description> "This document was prepared by Eclipse Energy Company Ltd in conjunction with Rudall Blanchard Associates. The report was submitted in support of the proposed Ormonde Offshore Wind Farm development and provides an extensive assessment of the potential impacts of the proposed site on the surrounding area. Included in the report are outlines of potential ecological, navigational and socio-economic impacts." .
_:fdc30a4d70655050550e41429f2f1bd3 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f185d93700621e5c1993b22fa226d8ee263f2691> <http://schema.org/description> "Preliminary survey work for the Shrimp trial project. Ground truthing was conducted using a video camera sled and day grab to assess and identify areas of subtidal mixed sediment within boxes identified as potentially suitable for the trial. The survey work was conducted across Wisbech Channel." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f185d93700621e5c1993b22fa226d8ee263f2691> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e71de156af5e090164a80ca7e4d75785 .
