<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ea773454aa5c9c7a1c80c8d35bc22c0f95af887e> <http://schema.org/description> "Drop Camera survey collecting video and still images of the seabed habitats within the Coquet to St Mary's rMCZ. Hamon Grab survey within the Coquet to St Mary's rMCZ. These data are archived with the Marine Environmental Data and Information Network (MEDIN) Data Archive Centres (DACs) including the British Geological Survey (BGS) DAC for geology and geophysics, The Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data (DASSH) and the United Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO) bathymetry DAC. The full site data package including raw is also available on request from BGS." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ea63aedf506d8cb14656dd63cc2a4eaddbd0d396> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset comprises hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, during August 1993. It incorporates a CTD survey of the Humber Estuary, Humber Plume, the Wash and Norfolk coastal waters and CTD sections E-W across the North Sea along 53N and 53.5N. The data were collected by the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Food Lowestoft Fisheries Laboratory as part of the Joint Nutrient Study I (JoNuS)." .
