_:b71311eb039e29901910a3653a71143e <http://schema.org/value> "south coast of England" .
_:ffb9e6b41b04988036bc4699aadeafbf <http://schema.org/value> "RSK" .
_:b71311eb039e29901910a3653a71143e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b71311eb039e29901910a3653a71143e <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:ffb9e6b41b04988036bc4699aadeafbf <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e5ad7f24c21e9b841f150e4eb62fd4247ee160d2> <http://schema.org/description> "A programme of monitoring has been undertaken by RSK in order to assess the potential noise\r\nimpacts at the residential receptors on the south coast of England, as a result of piling\r\nworks for the Rampion Offshore Wind Farm. The closest receptors to the piling works\r\nwill be properties along the coast, and will vary as different turbine bases are installed.\r\nThe closest piling works for construction of the wind farm bases will be taking place\r\napproximately 13.5km offshore.\r\nThe base for the meteorological mast was installed on 13 April 2012, using similar piling\r\ntechniques to those that will be employed for construction of the turbine bases. Noise\r\nmonitoring was undertaken on shore and on a boat close to the piling operations\r\nimmediately before, during, and after the piling operation, and noise level changes as a\r\nresult of the piling have been assessed." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e5ad7f24c21e9b841f150e4eb62fd4247ee160d2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e5ad7f24c21e9b841f150e4eb62fd4247ee160d2> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b71311eb039e29901910a3653a71143e .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e5a6bdd7c69956d443b105aa09442d31f4b9cb36> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:dfc2edc1f7516f29ec95a5386f85349 .
_:dfc2edc1f7516f29ec95a5386f85349 <http://schema.org/value> "Loch Paible" .
_:dfc2edc1f7516f29ec95a5386f85349 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:dfc2edc1f7516f29ec95a5386f85349 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e5a6bdd7c69956d443b105aa09442d31f4b9cb36> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e5a6bdd7c69956d443b105aa09442d31f4b9cb36> <http://schema.org/description> "The purpose of this study was to carry out site condition monitoring (SCM) of the mudflat feature within Loch Paible and biotope mapping of the sedimentary flats. SCM was inaugurated at this site in 2004, which provided a baseline for the current study. The principle aims were to: (1) identify any deterioration in the condition of the mudflat feature; and (2) to form a judgement on its current condition. The approach taken to achieve this aim was to resurvey two representative, relocatable transects established in 2004." .
_:fb1f675d0860e0a7dae38a99dfe54fb7 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e59f5961a846fa9cc5eb9b1bbf53237d40955c6d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e59f5961a846fa9cc5eb9b1bbf53237d40955c6d> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ac371fe5ed7a1fdd782b27fc0b43e49c .
_:c98eb3702ef9882296a99745dd39742f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ac371fe5ed7a1fdd782b27fc0b43e49c <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e59f5961a846fa9cc5eb9b1bbf53237d40955c6d> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c98eb3702ef9882296a99745dd39742f .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e59f5961a846fa9cc5eb9b1bbf53237d40955c6d> <http://schema.org/description> "A novel temperature dataset for northern high latitude Seas (ATLAS) is a dataset of three-dimensional temperature derived from combining quality controlled Argo float measurements with marine mammal mounted Satellite Relay Data Loggers (SRDLs) profiles. Using data values gathered from across the North Atlantic region, a 1×1 degree gridded temperature dataset of the average monthly values from January 2004 to December 2008, with 15 vertical layers between 0–700 m was produced. Built as complementary to existing ship-based fields, the ATLAS dataset is a community resource to help determine the impacts of climate change on the Labrador and Nordic Seas regions. The data were collated by the National Oceanography Centre (NOC) and are made available from the British Oceanographic Data Centre (BODC)." .
_:ac371fe5ed7a1fdd782b27fc0b43e49c <http://schema.org/value> "North Atlantic region" .
_:c98eb3702ef9882296a99745dd39742f <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
