_:d47dd14f91d175ca8677885520ad14a7 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e4ca5c85254a46469df6cc4411c4e74a83bd8965> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:d47dd14f91d175ca8677885520ad14a7 <http://schema.org/value> "Skegness" .
_:e1b889905832c1a3fddd567fa9a2fa59 <http://schema.org/value> "EGS International Ltd" .
_:d47dd14f91d175ca8677885520ad14a7 <http://schema.org/value> "southern North Sea" .
_:d47dd14f91d175ca8677885520ad14a7 <http://schema.org/value> "Lincolnshire" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e4ca5c85254a46469df6cc4411c4e74a83bd8965> <http://schema.org/description> "EGS International Ltd (EGSi) were contracted by Centrica Renewable Energy Limited (CREL) to\r\nundertake the 2015 post construction hydrographic and geophysical surveys of the Lincs and\r\nL&amp;ID (Lynn and Inner Dowsing) windfarm array cable routes.\r\nThe Lincs and L&amp;ID windfarms are located in the southern North Sea, approximately 5km off\r\nthe coast of Lincolnshire near Skegness. As an addition to the contracted 2015 survey work, a jack-up clearance survey was carried\r\nout in the Lincs wind farm at LS16, using Side-Scan Sonar (SSS) and Multibeam (MBES). Data\r\nused for this purpose was acquired on 1st-12th November (west of LS16) and 6th December\r\n(east of LS16).\r\nThis series details the operations and results of the survey around the LS16 turbine." .
_:d47dd14f91d175ca8677885520ad14a7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e1b889905832c1a3fddd567fa9a2fa59 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
