<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e130b02418309dd6e4965cc185b0359440cecbde> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:cbed964a15d4db3ab56de27b22331e7 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e130b02418309dd6e4965cc185b0359440cecbde> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e5191071e1eb8a94cc8806d81f45a66d .
_:e5191071e1eb8a94cc8806d81f45a66d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:cbed964a15d4db3ab56de27b22331e7 <http://schema.org/value> "Natural England" .
_:e5191071e1eb8a94cc8806d81f45a66d <http://schema.org/name> "marine species" .
_:fd24de1cbdd3bb3a76e6b7169655266e <http://schema.org/value> "nocturnal survey" .
_:e5191071e1eb8a94cc8806d81f45a66d <http://schema.org/value> "seabird" .
_:fd24de1cbdd3bb3a76e6b7169655266e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e130b02418309dd6e4965cc185b0359440cecbde> <http://schema.org/description> "RPS is advising RWE NRL on the assessment of the potential impacts on birds of\r\nthe proposed Atlantic Array offshore wind farm. Papers have been prepared and meetings have been held with the Countryside Council for Wales (CCW) and Natural England (NE) to discuss the risks that the proposed wind farm may pose to populations of birds (RPS 2010a) and on the development of the surveys to precede and inform the EIA (RPS 2010b). Three periods of sampling will be carried out overall, spanning the seabird breeding season. The report within this series provides information on the May survey only, with further surveys planned in July and September 2010.\r\nThe nocturnal survey had the primary objective of identifying if seabird flight activity (species, numbers, behaviour and height) differs significantly at night compared to that identified by the continuing programme of boat based diurnal surveys. The survey also provides information on other species or species groups but this information gathering was secondary to the primary objective." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e130b02418309dd6e4965cc185b0359440cecbde> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fd24de1cbdd3bb3a76e6b7169655266e .
_:cbed964a15d4db3ab56de27b22331e7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:cbed964a15d4db3ab56de27b22331e7 <http://schema.org/value> "Countryside Council for Wales" .
_:fd24de1cbdd3bb3a76e6b7169655266e <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
_:cbed964a15d4db3ab56de27b22331e7 <http://schema.org/value> "RPS" .
_:ac2dbed333a322e10d14b61dcc0ca7c8 <http://schema.org/value> "LDA Design" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e12dcbc81a4060a2de99ff77cd4abbd742d2c0c2> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ac2dbed333a322e10d14b61dcc0ca7c8 .
_:ac2dbed333a322e10d14b61dcc0ca7c8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e12dcbc81a4060a2de99ff77cd4abbd742d2c0c2> <http://schema.org/description> "This study forms chapter 16 of the Stage 2 Preliminary Environmental Information (Stage 2 PEI) of the Rhiannon Offshore Wind Farm, which is part of the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA). \r\nThe study was carried out by LDA Design and describes the existing environment with regard to Seascape, Landscape and Visual Amenity (SLVIA) and assesses the potential impacts of the Offshore Development area of the proposed Rhiannon Wind Farm (RWF).\r\nThe study assesses and describes:\r\n -The landscape and seascape planning policy context for the Offshore Development including a review of the key designations and planning policies relevant to the application site and the wider study area and the effects of the Offshore Development on these designations;\r\n -The seascape and landscape character of the study area, and the sensitivity of regional seascape units and landscape character areas/types at a national/regional and local scale; \r\n -The visual prominence of the Offshore Development and the sensitivity of representative visual receptors;\r\n -The magnitude of effect arising from the construction, operation and decommissioning of the Offshore Development;\r\n -The significance of the effects of the Offshore Development on seascape and landscape character, and on representative visual receptors; and\r\n -The cumulative effects of the Offshore Development to the identified baseline in combination with other onshore and offshore wind farms and infrastructure which are constructed/operational; and/or consented and in-planning/in-scoping within a 60km cumulative area of search.\r\n\r\nCorresponding Centrica Document No: \r\nSE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-016, SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-016-Att1, SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-016-Att2, SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-016-Att3, SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-016-Att4, SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-016-Att5\r\n\r\nAvailable Datasets : 1. ArcGIS files (mxds, . shapefiles), 2. Drawings (pdf, jpeg, png), \t3. Reports (.doc, .xls, .txt), \t4. Photos, (.tif) 5. Photomontage and Wireframe (pdf)\r\n\r\nPlease note reports are still in draft and Chapter 18 Archaeology and Cultural Heritage of Stage 2 Preliminary Environmental Information (Stage 2 PEI) of the Rhiannon Offshore Wind Farm is closely linked to this Seascape, Landscape and Visual Amenity (SLVIA) study" .
