_:ec245ed5242fd63ed6892e0dca0ac5c9 <http://schema.org/value> "measured sound levels" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e055a2f155196fa279355c074fdd3727028ca6aa> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ec245ed5242fd63ed6892e0dca0ac5c9 .
_:ec245ed5242fd63ed6892e0dca0ac5c9 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e055a2f155196fa279355c074fdd3727028ca6aa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e055a2f155196fa279355c074fdd3727028ca6aa> <http://schema.org/description> "This review primarily addresses the available information on windfarm related noise\r\nsources, with an emphasis on reported measured sound levels. Behavioural and\r\nphysical responses to noise are briefly covered where appropriate but are not treated\r\nin any great depth. Two sections are included, for readers unfamiliar with either\r\noffshore windfarms or underwater acoustics, which provide a sufficient background to\r\nunderstand the terms and concepts used in the review. These are followed by the\r\nbody of the report which contains a summary of the available information on\r\nwindfarm related noise sources." .
_:ec245ed5242fd63ed6892e0dca0ac5c9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ec245ed5242fd63ed6892e0dca0ac5c9 <http://schema.org/value> "depth" .
_:a956344e35e11d5e2dfaff0669fecd17 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ebd91178e3994186ec1082e232b085e2 <http://schema.org/value> "Noss Head" .
_:a956344e35e11d5e2dfaff0669fecd17 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e04e9a2c3fe9998fd47fbf35eef11c7ce8eaab9a> <http://schema.org/description> "The primary aim of this benthic survey at Noss Head, run by SNH and Marine Scotland Science (MSS) for SNH between the 8th and 12th July 2017 using MSS vessel MRV Alba na Mara (cruise 1117A), was to improve knowledge of protected features within the MPA and biotope distribution out with the MPA. This 1117A survey is part of a series of surveys conducted around the North-east coast of Scotland, at Noss Head, Moray Firth and Southern Trench, to establish the extent of benthic habitats. Quantitative drop-down camera sampling was used to collect this data at 126 stations at Noss Head. Through the analysis of seabed video, the images were used to describe the nature of the seabed in terms of the physical structure and the species assemblages. Runs and run segments were assessed for the presence of protected features and other PMFs, as well as for the presence of species and habitats of recognised conservation importance." .
_:ebd91178e3994186ec1082e232b085e2 <http://schema.org/value> "North-east coast of Scotland" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e04e9a2c3fe9998fd47fbf35eef11c7ce8eaab9a> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a956344e35e11d5e2dfaff0669fecd17 .
