<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:dc7f481af14a57e2486e52ada7c5e68f28f905c3> <http://schema.org/description> "This study assessed the scope of the existing sustainable development strategy (SDS) developed by the British Marine Aggregate Producers Association (BMAPA). Gaps in the strategy are identified, particularly in relation to existing and developing legislation, and recommendations made for further core values, indicators and targets. The study improves on the existing framework of indicators, incorporating the requirements of European Directives (Habitats, Birds and Water Framework Directives), Sustainable Development strategies and predictions on future requirements under Marine Spatial Planning and MSFD." .
_:f5881140b03886e57dbb267fb2a9d29b <http://schema.org/value> "MSFD" .
_:a67cd27635cfd5fa223ab83a18b34a2a <http://schema.org/value> "British Marine Aggregate Producers Association" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:dc7c4d04a389843271513aca668d46488f8b8840> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset contains information on the SACFOR abundance of benthic infauna species from video footage from Skerries and Causeway Special Areas of Conservation (SAC) in Northern Irish waters. The selected SACâ??s have previous multibeam data available for each site, therefore this project was to provide ground-truthing evidence for these habitats. This survey took place on 2017-09-27 on board the RV Corystes. A towed sledge camera was used in this survey. The video sledge was attached by a 400m cable with a USBL system, scaling lasers and an ancillary GoPro. A 0.1m2 day grab was also used as further ground-truthing but this information is not included in this dataset. Particle size analysis and Carbon and Nitrogen analysis were also carried out (not included in this dataset). Information on the substrate was collected and is included in this dataset." .
