<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:d8943086a27c8743b851570ac7904d1e2e6da601> <http://schema.org/description> "The Teesside A and B Fish and Shellfish Technical Report provides a description of the existing environment in the area of the proposed Dogger Bank Teesside A &amp; B offshore wind farms and the Dogger Bank Teesside A &amp; B Export Cable Corridor in relation to fish and shellfish resources and ecology. It provides supporting information to the Fish and Shellfish Environmental Statement (Chapter 13) and has been undertaken by Brown and May Marine Ltd.\r\n\r\nESRI ArcGIS software has been used to present the data within the report." .
_:e2f7945120f6e121f116b4caddd16744 <http://schema.org/value> "Brown and May Marine Ltd." .
_:d4bf3e4708ac48c5627163f8794ec27b <http://schema.org/value> "Scottish Marine Biological Association" .
_:a5da830df554c4e5fcb92430e8aef20 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:d88b5be1c41361954185f257d8c8950783000187> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a5da830df554c4e5fcb92430e8aef20 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:d88b5be1c41361954185f257d8c8950783000187> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 3 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, in the North East Atlantic Ocean. Two of these were on the Ellett Line between the Anton Dohrn Seamount and Rockall. The third cast was performed in the Little Minch. The data were collected during October of 1982. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Scottish Marine Biological Association." .
_:d4bf3e4708ac48c5627163f8794ec27b <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
