_:d11c0efcae9209da939a4a8998560dbe <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:d7556309623a8c3408bf02fcd124a69873654e17> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:d11c0efcae9209da939a4a8998560dbe <http://schema.org/value> "Shetland Islands" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:d7556309623a8c3408bf02fcd124a69873654e17> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 47 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the North Sea area specifically across the Northern North Sea and around the Shetland Islands, during January and February of 2002. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Fisheries Research Services Aberdeen Marine Laboratory." .
_:d11c0efcae9209da939a4a8998560dbe <http://schema.org/value> "North Sea area" .
_:cdc0ba57698ed33de6f65a18286e2f7f <http://schema.org/value> "hydrographic data profiles" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:d741dbfd4ad2bb777cc75279b49f1eaaef22e8fb> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset presents the results of a Desk Study carried out by METOC to inform the feasibility of a Horizontal Directional Drilling (HDD) crossing for the landfall of the Atlantic Array wind farm export cables at Cornborough on the North Devon coast. The Cornborough Range landfall has been selected as the favoured option by RWE. It is proposed that a sixty metre swath containing between six and ten 132 kVA cables will cross the foreshore at Cornborough. The preferred method of crossing this area to avoid environmental disturbance, is HDD. The landfall, sub-surface route section at Cornborough is considered feasible from a geological viewpoint. Considerable attention, however, will be required in assessing the profile of the tunnels in order to ensure the drill profile is, if possible, entirely within unweathered rock and avoiding all mapped faults and fractures, and ideally exiting offshore in soft sediments." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:d741dbfd4ad2bb777cc75279b49f1eaaef22e8fb> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bdad5e08e36aa832790fcb3e282d3904 .
_:daf32d4bc2147a86d7d662420959e2bb <http://schema.org/value> "Cornborough" .
_:daf32d4bc2147a86d7d662420959e2bb <http://schema.org/value> "North Devon coast" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:d741dbfd4ad2bb777cc75279b49f1eaaef22e8fb> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:daf32d4bc2147a86d7d662420959e2bb .
_:bdad5e08e36aa832790fcb3e282d3904 <http://schema.org/value> "RWE" .
