<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:d36a732fdccb3373b18e77434bf7ea4ea88ce2ae> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 61 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the Inner Seas off the west coast of Scotland area specifically the Firth of Clyde and the North Channel, during April and May of 1989. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Scottish Office Agriculture and Fisheries Department Aberdeen Marine Laboratory." .
