_:c9ba3bf8494357241a5af024c79f1f48 <http://schema.org/value> "RPS Planning Transport and Environment" .
_:c9ba3bf8494357241a5af024c79f1f48 <http://schema.org/value> "National Grid" .
_:c9ba3bf8494357241a5af024c79f1f48 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cae81d05495662191a5b83ba9a7744b32a202730> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cae81d05495662191a5b83ba9a7744b32a202730> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:dc8e1b25c39b22d69ebf992be8f24b0c .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cae81d05495662191a5b83ba9a7744b32a202730> <http://schema.org/description> "RPS Planning Transport and Environment (RPS) were commissioned to undertake a\r\nFlood Risk Assessment (FRA) for the laying of electrical cables from three offshore wind farms\r\nto an existing electrical substation at Walpole. Centrica Renewable Energy Limited\r\n(CREL) will need to extend the substation at Walpole. National Grid (NG) will also be required\r\nto extend their part of this substation to accommodate the CREL works. This FRA considers the flood risk and impacts upon the surface-water runoff regime from the laying of cables. A cumulative assessment from the proposed extension works at Walpole electrical substation has also been conducted." .
_:dc8e1b25c39b22d69ebf992be8f24b0c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b69128c6b5c49331c0ecd8e7952e1bd1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c0ff2eb2f73125a1f36397b37a8159e7 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:adac9bbb03579aedbf4f3c8d9495cf2e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b69128c6b5c49331c0ecd8e7952e1bd1 <http://schema.org/value> "presence records" .
_:c0ff2eb2f73125a1f36397b37a8159e7 <http://schema.org/value> "Devon" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cae37cd24b087b8e917d1a59ca01ede0dc1ffec4> <http://schema.org/description> "Sabellaria alveolata presence records from an intertidal survey of Devon and Cornwall. The report does not specify the means by which samples were obtained nor specific geographical locations. The latter had to be therefore estimated and are presented by an estimate of area coverage." .
