<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:c7dc0bedf5028c34470aea97e4bb47c435839842> <http://schema.org/description> "To expand on the 2020 DSIFCA Taw Torridge subtidal mussel survey, a side scan sonar (SSS) and grab survey was carried out in 2021. This was undertaken to gain a better understanding of the extent of the subtidal mussel beds. As this was the first time DSIFCA have used the SSS methodology, proof of concept was a secondary objective of the project. A Tritech SeaKing Towfish SSS was deployed on the 14th October 2021 for a total of 13 transects of different lengths throughout the Estuary. This data was then analysed to plan the grab stations for ground-truthing the SSS signature, with 45 grab stations being identified. A total of 89 grabs were carried out across the stations on the 15th October 2021, with an Offset Day Grab with a sampling area of 0.1mÂ². The survey was carried out by a DSIFCA and a Cornwall IFCA officer on board a local fishing vessel. Data includes georeferenced SSS tracks, georefenced grab success/failure, count of mussel in each grab and mussel length data for all mussels collected in grabs." .
_:a204ff6d880d9debd0a2a3eb062bf015 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:f29b75446a7debcb110dab0b5e396cea <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:b2231ce1a973d850b4d90d1107fdb1e5 <http://schema.org/value> "Northern Ireland" .
_:f29b75446a7debcb110dab0b5e396cea <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:f29b75446a7debcb110dab0b5e396cea <http://schema.org/value> "Environment Agency" .
_:b2231ce1a973d850b4d90d1107fdb1e5 <http://schema.org/value> "UK" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:c7d4ac2b5e8e3a61dbcf4486c7bcbf36d2080639> <http://schema.org/description> "The Bathing Water Directive 2006/7/EC (BWD) sets quality standards for bathing water. Countries in the European Union must ensure that their bathing waters meets these standards. \r\n In Northern Ireland, 26 sites are formally identified under the BWD. Bathing water quality is monitored by DAERA Marine and Fisheries Division. The bathing season runs from June through to mid-September. Water quality is assessed on 19 occasions during the season and one occasion pre-season. Water samples are collected and analysed for the required microbiological standards. Bathing Water Quality information is updated weekly during the bathing season and displayed at the bathing waters and on the DAERA website. The annual data is forwarded to the Environment Agency (EA) at the end of each bathing season. The EA compiles all data from the UK and forwards on to the European Commission. Compliance against the BWD is calculated by DAERA Marine and Fisheries on a four year rolling data set." .
_:b2231ce1a973d850b4d90d1107fdb1e5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:c7d4ac2b5e8e3a61dbcf4486c7bcbf36d2080639> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b2231ce1a973d850b4d90d1107fdb1e5 .
