<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:bab7f4d706fa6c839c6fa954db7d97426e94dc02> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b23b32f77e92afd1d9583a2d988733b2 .
_:b23b32f77e92afd1d9583a2d988733b2 <http://schema.org/value> "Maritime Archaeology Ltd" .
_:f70aa507d2d2d9e31bce53751425c93f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:f70aa507d2d2d9e31bce53751425c93f <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ba8f549e848e038bf9dd443115377c74b39f45e0> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology was commissioned by Forewind to undertake an archaeological assessment for the first two of four Dogger Bank Teesside wind farms and associated export cables: Dogger Bank Teesside A and Dogger Bank Teesside B. Assessment was carried out within defined Study Areas comprising the project\r\nboundaries, export cable corridor and Temporary Working Areas (1km around the Dogger\r\nBank Teesside project boundaries and 750m either side of the Dogger Bank Teesside A and\r\nB Export Cable Corridor).\r\nThe principle sources for data comprised geophysical and geotechnical survey datasets\r\ngathered for the current development, records held by the United Kingdom Hydrographic\r\nOffice, the National Record of the Historic Environment and the Redcar and Cleveland\r\nHistoric Environment Record, and secondary sources relating to previous archaeological\r\nand geophysical work in the region." .
_:f70aa507d2d2d9e31bce53751425c93f <http://schema.org/value> "Forewind" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ba8f549e848e038bf9dd443115377c74b39f45e0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ba8f549e848e038bf9dd443115377c74b39f45e0> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f70aa507d2d2d9e31bce53751425c93f .
_:f70aa507d2d2d9e31bce53751425c93f <http://schema.org/value> "Wessex Archaeology" .
