<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b84f6c378509146d19d44a786feacd53ddcdea12> <http://schema.org/description> "This is a digitised version of the third edition of the Plymouth Marine Fauna. It contains a complete list of every fauna species found from Exmouth to Dodman Point (near Penare, Cornwall) as of its publication in 1957. In general the area covered by the list stretches along the coast from Start Point in Devon to Looe in Cornwall and southwards to the outer Channel grounds. In addition, records are included for Salcombe, Torbay and Exmouth, and very occasionally elsewhere, such as the north coast of Cornwall. This edition was edited by Dr. D.P. Wilson and Mr. G.M. Spooner. The following are the names of those who have been responsible for the revision of the records of the different species in their respective groups. These are arranged in the order in which the groups are printed in the fauna list. Mastigophora (Dr. L. E. R. Picken); Foraminifera (Mr. C. D. Ovey); Acantharia, Radiolaria, Heliozoa (Dr. L. E. R. Picken); Sporozoa (Dr. Helen P. Goodrich); Ciliophora (Dr. Maria Felinska); Mesozoa (Dr. D. Atkins); Porifera (Dr. M. Burton, with additions by Mr. G. R. Forster); Hydroida (Dr. W. J. Rees); Hydromedusae (Dr. F. S. Russell, F.R.S.); Siphonophora (Captain A. K. Totton and Dr. F. S. Russell, F.R.S.); Scyphomedusae (Dr. F. S. Russell, F.R.S.); Stauromedusae (Mr. P. G. Corbin); Alcyonacea, Gorgonacea, Pennatulacea, Ceriantharia, Zoantharia (checked by Prof. C. M. Yonge, F.R.S.); Actiniaria (Prof. T. A. Stephenson, F.R.S.); Madreporaria, Corallimorpharia (checked by Prof. C. M. Yonge, F. R. S.); Turbellaria (Dr. C. F. A. Pantin, F.R.S.); Polycladida (Mr. S. Prudhoe); Trematoda, Cestoda (Mr. S. Prudhoe and Dr. H. A. Bayliss); free-living Nematoda (Dr. W. Wieser); parasitic Nematoda (Mr. S. Prudhoe and Dr. H. A. Bayliss); Acanthocephala (Mr. S. Prudhoe and Dr. H. A. Bayliss); Rotifera (Mr. E. D. Hollowday); Nemertini (Dr. C. F. A. Pantin, F.R.S); Annelida (Dr. D. P. Wilson and Mr. N. Tebble); Echiuroidea, Sipunculoidea (Dr. A. C. Stephen); Branchiopoda, Ostracoda, Copepoda (Dr. J. P. Harding); Cirripedia (Dr. J. P. Harding with additions by Dr. A. J. Southward); Leptostraca, Stomatopoda, Cumacea (Dr. J. P. Harding); Tanaidacea, Isopoda, Amphipoda (Mr. G. M. Spooner); Schizopoda (Dr. Olive S. Tattersall); Eucarida (Dr. Isabella Gordon); Acarina, Pseudoscorpionidea (Mr. G. M. Spooner); Pycnogonida (Dr. Marie V. Lebour); Myriapoda, Insecta (Mr. G. M. Spooner); Mollusca (Originally revised by the late Mr. R. Winckworth, more recently by Prof. A. Graham and Dr. Vera Fretter); Nudibranchia (Dr. J. E. Forrest); Cephalopoda (Dr. W. J. Rees); Chaetognatha (Dr. F. S. Russell, F.R.S.); Phoronidea (Dr. Eve C. Southward); Kamptozoa, Polyzoa (Dr. Anna B. Hastings); Echinodermata (Dr. H. G. Vevers); Hemichordata (Dr. C. Burdon Jones); Tunicata (Prof. N. J. Berrill, F.R.S., with additions by Dr. D. B. Carlisle); Thaliacea and Copelata (Dr. F. S. Russell, F.R.S.); Vertebrata (Dr. G. A. Steven with the assistance of Dr. E. Trewavas and Mr. D. W. Tucker); Ammodytidae (Mr. P. G. Corbin; additions by Mr. E. Ford and Mr. P. G. Corbin)." .
