_:beee46e68e7919b15a219f64db2df981 <http://schema.org/value> "Eneco Round 3 Development Ltd." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b42d493c3cfd1a63e94cbcbf928b1894412fd5ec> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:beee46e68e7919b15a219f64db2df981 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b42d493c3cfd1a63e94cbcbf928b1894412fd5ec> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d9aebc8dd74742a43bd6e697c5b53a8e .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b42d493c3cfd1a63e94cbcbf928b1894412fd5ec> <http://schema.org/description> "Eneco Round 3 Development Ltd. (Eneco) in the United Kingdom is developing Zone 7 (Navitus Bay), which is one of the Crown Estate Round 3 offshore wind farm zones. An area within Zone 7, Lot 1 (West Isle of Wight), has been selected for wind farm development. Eneco has contracted Fugro Survey BV (FSBV) to perform a detailed geophysical survey of the Lot 1 site, together with two (2) potential export cable routes to the UK mainland. The location of the project site and the potential export cable routes are shown in Figure 1. The geophysical survey was conducted between 25 July 2011 and 25 August 2011 from the survey vessel M.V. Aurelia, deploying the following equipment: - A single beam echo sounder (SBE) - A multi beam echo sounder (MBES), - A ultra high resolution portable multi channel seismic profiling system (UHR) - A high resolution side scan sonar (SSS). - A sub bottom profiler (SBP) - A magnetometer (MM) In Lot 2, the two export cable routes, the same equipment was deployed excluding the UHR system.\r\nThis series contains Bathymetry, Magnetometer, Side Scan Sonar, SMT Kingdon project, Sound Velocity profiles, Sub-bottom profilers and UHR Seismic data from the survey." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b42d493c3cfd1a63e94cbcbf928b1894412fd5ec> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:beee46e68e7919b15a219f64db2df981 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b42d493c3cfd1a63e94cbcbf928b1894412fd5ec> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c19e3c2ff8a1fac32b0d1fd4fb8e50ff .
_:c19e3c2ff8a1fac32b0d1fd4fb8e50ff <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
_:d9aebc8dd74742a43bd6e697c5b53a8e <http://schema.org/value> "Zone 7" .
_:beee46e68e7919b15a219f64db2df981 <http://schema.org/value> "Fugro Survey BV" .
_:eb1e63d6071348684c1148728e5f859a <http://schema.org/value> "EGS (International) Ltd" .
_:eb1e63d6071348684c1148728e5f859a <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b41f1696d2f927e28d3e0cafb26fb42108f3c8c6> <http://schema.org/description> "In May 2012 EGS (International) Ltd was contracted to undertake a bathymetric survey in\r\nthe post-construction (operational) phase of the project to determine whether there are\r\nany changes to seabed morphology at the wind farm site including inter array cables. The\r\nsurvey covered all turbine foundations using a corridor 370 metre wide along the array\r\ncables connecting the turbines.\r\nTo meet this objective EGS conducted a multibeam high frequency bathymetric survey\r\ncombined with seabed mapping and sub-surface hazard identification using side-scan sonar\r\n(SSS) in conjunction with a USBL system, across each of the constructed WTG and substation\r\nlocation over the Barrow Offshore Windfarm.\r\nSurvey operations over the site were completed with the EGS Pioneer on a 24 hour\r\noperational basis between 17th and 18th May 2012." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b41f1696d2f927e28d3e0cafb26fb42108f3c8c6> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:eb1e63d6071348684c1148728e5f859a .
