_:aca29124ca157396c2891ee8cac9d38f <http://schema.org/value> "Liverpool Bay area" .
_:b53c5c94710410bf2a6bba06a563a155 <http://schema.org/value> "Coastal and Intertidal Zone Archaeological Network" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b1eedb7dda70960925d8c3556f42b8e71eafdb07> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:aca29124ca157396c2891ee8cac9d38f .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b1eedb7dda70960925d8c3556f42b8e71eafdb07> <http://schema.org/description> "This collection comprises images, GIS, and spreadsheet data from a coastal erosion survey of the tobacco dumping area (known locally as the Tobacco Cliffs) undertaken by Coastal and Intertidal Zone Archaeological Network's (CITiZAN) staff and volunteers between November 2015 and April 2022, as part of a programme to monitor coastal and intertidal archaeological features within the Liverpool Bay area." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b1eedb7dda70960925d8c3556f42b8e71eafdb07> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b1de6d95c7c40ed05cf2b055481aba3580510ef0> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c0cd1a5b8e9367e6c0c46fd0ab26f333 .
_:c0cd1a5b8e9367e6c0c46fd0ab26f333 <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
_:c0cd1a5b8e9367e6c0c46fd0ab26f333 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b1de6d95c7c40ed05cf2b055481aba3580510ef0> <http://schema.org/description> "This project relates to the effect of the underwater noise generated during the construction of the Lynn and Inner Dowsing wind farms on marine mammals. A specific Marine Mammal Monitoring Protocol was adopted to ensure no marine mammals were within 500 metres of the pile during the 30 minutes preceding the start of piling. Acoustic mitigation monitoring data was collected for 85 hours and visual mitigation monitoring data was collected for 82 hours. Recommendations are made for the improvement of the protocol and soft start procedures - including a refining of the soft start procedure and the use of acoustic deterrent devices during night time starts." .
_:c0cd1a5b8e9367e6c0c46fd0ab26f333 <http://schema.org/value> "soft start procedures" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b1de6d95c7c40ed05cf2b055481aba3580510ef0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:dd95db4f363b56efabb270a279812de7 <http://schema.org/value> "Osiris Projects" .
_:dd95db4f363b56efabb270a279812de7 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b1b0a8c6aa88cd118a213286987767699b14e4a1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c1a01e0cb6bc8fa3c1a4f6462f897d38 .
_:c1a01e0cb6bc8fa3c1a4f6462f897d38 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:c1a01e0cb6bc8fa3c1a4f6462f897d38 <http://schema.org/value> "RPS Explosives Engineering Services" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b1b0a8c6aa88cd118a213286987767699b14e4a1> <http://schema.org/description> "The proposed Lincs Offshore Wind Farm (OWR) developed by Centrica Energy, lies\r\non the eastern (seaward) side of the consented Lynn and Inner Dowsing wind farms,\r\napproximately 8-12km off the coast of Lincolnshire. Two export cables will connect\r\nthe wind farm to the grid, with landfall to the east of the mouth of the River Nene.\r\nThe region has been historically subjected to a legacy of military activity that is likely\r\nto have resulted in unexploded ordnance (UXO) contamination.\r\nOn behalf of Centrica Energy, Emu Limited and Osiris Projects conducted\r\ngeophysical surveys along the Lincs Export Cable Route. The purpose of the\r\nsurveys was to identify the presence of any debris or obstructions along the route.\r\nMoreover to obtaining suitable morphology and geological information on seabed\r\nbathymetry, seabed features and sub-seabed conditions. There was no\r\nconsideration to plan for a full UXO survey at the time and the subsequent data\r\nprocessing did not consider this issue.\r\nRPS Explosives Engineering Services (EES) have now been commissioned to\r\nreview 26 geophysical contacts / sites that have been highlighted by Wessex\r\nArchaeology to determine whether an UXO assessment can be undertaken." .
_:aeba8a53f60d25be0ec7b801cc50b010 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d3cb356b4a03a02cc83137eefad1e80a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
