<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:adb093c9236eb24e850329b78b3df46bb46941dd> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e39a8fd0f84564cbf191e94dfab0cb37 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:adb093c9236eb24e850329b78b3df46bb46941dd> <http://schema.org/description> "The East Yorkshire to Norfolk HSC project forms part of a larger programme implementing Historic Seascape Characterisation (HSC) across England's coastal and marine areas. It does this by mapping the historic character of the present-day coastal and marine environment, using many of the same principles as its sister project, Historic Landscape Characterisation (HLC). This study was commissioned from Newcastle University by English Heritage as a part of the National Heritage Protection Plan (NHPP) Activity 3A1 on Identifying unknown marine Assets and Landscapes, to undertake a Historic Seascape Characterisation (HSC) across the areas of England's coast and English Inshore and Offshore regions, contributing to English Heritage's national HSC database. This report is divided into three sections for ease of use." .
_:f223e4518dff4f9d4b91791481a50d87 <http://schema.org/name> "dna sequences" .
_:f223e4518dff4f9d4b91791481a50d87 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ada87efbabe869d1f86276f4d6a9de794bdc5161> <http://schema.org/description> "1971 - 2015 Dove Marine Laboratory Benthic Station P (North Sea) Time Series Data. Benthic samples taken from Station P, 18.5 km off the North - East coast of England, using a 0.1m2 Van Veen grab, since January 1971, initially at 2 monthly intervals (1971) with 30 replicates taken. The frequencies of sampling occurrences declined to one sampling occurrence in January - March with five replicates taken per occurrence until 2015. The samples are sieved over a 0.5mm mesh and fixed in formaldehyde. The samples are processed in the lab and fauna is extracted and identified to species level, where possible, in abundance per square metre. Sample collection and data processing and publication was finalised in 2015. \r\n Benthic sampling has been re-initiated in March 2021, with PSA and sediment for eDNA taken." .
