<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a8e1d35ff09cfb893f08d2aff56b6d042c831046> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 126 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, within the North East Atlantic Ocean area. It incorporates the Dunstaffnage Marine Laboratory Rockall via Anton Dohrn Seamount (Ellett Line) section, plus further shelf sections covering the North Channel, channels between the Hebrides and the mainland and the shelf between the Outer Hebrides and the shelf edge. The data were collected during June and July of 1984. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Scottish Marine Biological Association." .
_:f2dfe44bcd5edb1d20879a127102fe6b <http://schema.org/value> "Scottish Marine Biological Association" .
_:d99a0b8ab5dddac72003aa9464526c53 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d99a0b8ab5dddac72003aa9464526c53 <http://schema.org/value> "Skerries Tidal Array" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a8b84da4938765cd73147b21aa8efedeb24b2933> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b420e4306a41956d7d81292902363f82 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a8b84da4938765cd73147b21aa8efedeb24b2933> <http://schema.org/description> "This study assesses the navigational risk of installing an export cable route from the Skerries Tidal Array and complements the existing Navigation Risk Assessment\r\n\r\nThe assessment was undertaken utilising the Formal Safety Assessment approach adopted by the International Maritime Organisation. The analysis uitilised a number of data sources including vessel traffic surveys, records of consultation with relevant stakeholders undertaken during the Navigation Risk Assessment and a desktop literature review." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a8b84da4938765cd73147b21aa8efedeb24b2933> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
