_:d1b11d52ee847b7b38ab8d4a08934155 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:a38e39d1fd20100718a21a674ee23831 <http://schema.org/value> "Wessex Archaeology" .
_:a38e39d1fd20100718a21a674ee23831 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a56221b5841cdcd11a0e19bbf3e8f8d9f5da0f56> <http://schema.org/description> "This project examines the Archaeological Protocol that has been prepared by Wessex Archaeology for the development stage of the Barrow offshore wind farm. The protocol is based on recommendations made in the Environmental Assessment Technical Report. The responsibility of implementing the protocol rests with Vestas-KBR. Construction exclusion zones will be the principle means used to preserve in situ any deposits of potential or known archaeological interest. These zones will be periodically monitored by visits from an appropriately qualified archaeologist. Geophysical, geotechnical, diver/ROV observations and walk over surveys will help identify archaeological features and if necessary alter the construction exclusion zones." .
_:a38e39d1fd20100718a21a674ee23831 <http://schema.org/value> "Vestas-KBR" .
_:a625292bac7b1ce7aac0c6d8cdd25fc2 <http://schema.org/value> "Multibeam (MBES)" .
_:a960ec7edfb7be50a0a7a787f401566c <http://schema.org/value> "WTGs LS28" .
_:a625292bac7b1ce7aac0c6d8cdd25fc2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a529004a6f9b84b0d9dc67ba669a17bfba248e8a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a529004a6f9b84b0d9dc67ba669a17bfba248e8a> <http://schema.org/description> "EGS (International) Ltd, on behalf of Centrica, undertook a Side-Scan Sonar (SSS) and\r\nMultibeam (MBES) clearance survey centered on the no cable zones (500m by 500m) around\r\nWTGs LS28 (on the Lincs site), and ID16 and ID24 (on the Inner Dowsing Site). The areas\r\nsurveyed were identified by Centrica for the upcoming works on the aforementioned turbines\r\nand respond to the need to have a jack-up vessel in the locality to complete the works. This\r\nseries details the operations and results of the survey around all turbines. Please note the data provided within this series only covers the Lincs site, whilst the report covers both the Lincs and Inner Dowsing Offshore Wind Farms." .
_:d598615b2655f7146dc052e0ffa851ad <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:a960ec7edfb7be50a0a7a787f401566c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
