_:c4aa4a3a3d615b01dd23961b31e6ab0c <http://schema.org/value> "chlorophyll profiles" .
_:b7046178ee68e4f332a621e35b7c9397 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:daf3e367be7ccce143bf80be6f1513da <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:95638c90b6b682ed81024cffd2406d41696c42b6> <http://schema.org/description> "The data set includes Sea Rover undulating oceanographic recorder data, including temperature, salinity and chlorophyll profiles. The data were collected in the North Atlantic during the 1980s. Data collection was undertaken along numerous sections between 1981 and 1987, as follows: 1981 - 5 sections and polar front box survey; 1983 - 5 sections and polar front box survey; 1984 - 6 sections; 1985 - 3 sections; 1986 - 4 sections; 1987 - 2 sections. The sections vary in length between 500 and 1000 miles and the data includes a number of repeated traverses between the Azores and the Ocean Weather Ship at Station 'Charlie'. The data were collected by the Institut fur Meereskunde, Kiel and have been assembled by the British Oceanographic Data Centre." .
_:c4aa4a3a3d615b01dd23961b31e6ab0c <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
_:b7046178ee68e4f332a621e35b7c9397 <http://schema.org/value> "British Oceanographic Data Centre" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9563376586528469a7090aaa0110055a65bd3d0a> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 102 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the North Sea area specifically the east coast of Scotland, during April of 1992. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Scottish Office Agriculture and Fisheries Department Aberdeen Marine Laboratory." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9563376586528469a7090aaa0110055a65bd3d0a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
