<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:93d63b93c0f4e2a339e65905ee57051417cf9d9f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:cb5fdfa9aa653b3a74b5c82826ad3f35 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:93d63b93c0f4e2a339e65905ee57051417cf9d9f> <http://schema.org/description> "Multibeam survey collecting bathymetry and backscatter to give full coverage with existing coverage from previous survey in 20XX. WGS84 latitude and longitude co-ordinates collected by Differential Global Positioning System (D-GPS), depths corrected to Chart Datum (CD). Raw and processed data delivered to Centre for Environment, Fisheries and Aquaculture Science, UK (Cefas) complete with georeferenced mosaics and GeoTiffs images. Drop Camera collecting video and still images of the seabed habitats within Cape Bank rMCZ.Grab survey collecting PSA and benthin infaunal samples from seabed habitats within Cape Bank rMCZ. These data are archived with the Marine Environmental Data and Information Network (MEDIN) Data Archive Centres (DACs) including the British Geological Survey (BGS) DAC for geology and geophysics, The Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data (DASSH) and the United Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO) bathymetry DAC.The full site data package (excluding raw bathymetry) is also available on request from BGS." .
_:c6d22c112565acd23f281d36cc66f2cd <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:c6d22c112565acd23f281d36cc66f2cd <http://schema.org/value> "Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data" .
_:c6d22c112565acd23f281d36cc66f2cd <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey" .
_:c6d22c112565acd23f281d36cc66f2cd <http://schema.org/value> "United Kingdom Hydrographic Office" .
_:cb5fdfa9aa653b3a74b5c82826ad3f35 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:93afa71746ea386fa846d86c3d4639bda4c5a553> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset comprises hydrographic data profiles, collected by a salinity-temperature-depth (STD) sensor package, in July 1978. It incorporates triangular surveys around each of the Joint Air Sea Interaction Experiment (JASIN) moorings NW of the Anton Dohrn Seamount. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Scottish Marine Biological Association." .
