_:d752d2dc96a6272df917537a4ae99ed0 <http://schema.org/value> "North Channel" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:901554f20d2ef3f7d30b0250ef468f3b816900ce> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 115 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, within the North East Atlantic Ocean area. It incorporates stations of the Dunstaffnage Marine Laboratory Rockall via Anton Dohrn Seamount (Ellett Line), plus sections in the North Channel, westward from Islay, between Lewis and the mainland and an extensive grid of stations in the Firth of Clyde, Kilbrannan Sound and Lower Loch Fyne. The data were collected during January and February of 1985. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Scottish Marine Biological Association." .
