<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8b031ec65c5efba6787c0eee87bc8afbc3f24939> <http://schema.org/description> "Volunteer divers recorded species observations on record cards for the Underwater Observation Scheme established in 1977 as part of the Underwater Conservation Year. This dataset represents the records card collected in MNCR Sector UK08, West English Channel." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8aeff2a4f268858c17f4817f3e25b994fde13b6e> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:be9762bff03bb5a7c428a1c7de8f59d0 .
_:be9762bff03bb5a7c428a1c7de8f59d0 <http://schema.org/value> "United Kingdom Hydrographic Office" .
_:be9762bff03bb5a7c428a1c7de8f59d0 <http://schema.org/value> "Marine Environmental Data and Information Network" .
_:be9762bff03bb5a7c428a1c7de8f59d0 <http://schema.org/value> "Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data" .
_:be9762bff03bb5a7c428a1c7de8f59d0 <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8aeff2a4f268858c17f4817f3e25b994fde13b6e> <http://schema.org/description> "Full coverage multibeam survey collecting bathymetry and backscatter to client specifications, namely International Hydrographic Organization (IHO) Order 1a standard, WGS84 latitude and longitude co-ordinates collected by Differential Global Navigation Satellite System (DGNSS), depths corrected to Chart Datum (CD), full seafloor coverage achieved. Raw and processed data delivered to Centre for Environment, Fisheries and Aquaculture Science, UK (Cefas) complete with georeferenced mosaics and GeoTiffs images. These data are archived with the Marine Environmental Data and Information Network (MEDIN) Data Archive Centres (DACs) including the British Geological Survey (BGS) DAC for geology and geophysics, The Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data (DASSH) and the United Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO) bathymetry DAC. The full site data package including raw is also available on request from BGS." .
_:be9762bff03bb5a7c428a1c7de8f59d0 <http://schema.org/value> "Centre for Environment, Fisheries and Aquaculture Science" .
_:be9762bff03bb5a7c428a1c7de8f59d0 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8aeff2a4f268858c17f4817f3e25b994fde13b6e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:be9762bff03bb5a7c428a1c7de8f59d0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:cf745e727a02ea13a63f129cd18acc1c <http://schema.org/value> "Naval Postgraduate School" .
_:cf745e727a02ea13a63f129cd18acc1c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:cf745e727a02ea13a63f129cd18acc1c <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8ae6cb145c8ff0a7aa797dd35aafe8b9c9d09299> <http://schema.org/description> "The World Ocean Isopycnal-Level Velocity (WOIL-V) climatology was derived from the United States Navy's Generalised Digital Environmental Model (GDEM) temperature and salinity profiles, using the P-Vector Method. The absolute velocity data have the same horizontal resolution and temporal variation (annual, monthly) as GDEM (T, S) fields. These data have an horizontal resolution of 0.5 degrees ×0.5 degrees, and 222 isopycnal-levels (sigma theta levels) from sigma theta = 22.200 to 27.725 (kg m-3) with the increment delta sigma theta = 0.025 (kg m-3), however in the equatorial zone (5 degrees S – 5 degrees N) they are questionable due to the geostrophic balance being the theoretical base for the P-vector inverse method. The GDEM model, which served as the base for the calculations includes data from 1920s onwards and the WOIL-V will be updated with the same frequency as the GDEM. The climatological velocity field on isopycnal surface is dynamically compatible to the GDEM (T, S) fields and provides background ocean currents for oceanographic and climatic studies, especially in ocean isopycnal modeling. The climatology was prepared by the Department of Oceanography, Naval Postgraduate School." .
_:cf745e727a02ea13a63f129cd18acc1c <http://schema.org/value> "Department of Oceanography" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8ae6cb145c8ff0a7aa797dd35aafe8b9c9d09299> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:cf745e727a02ea13a63f129cd18acc1c .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8ae6cb145c8ff0a7aa797dd35aafe8b9c9d09299> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:ce70941e050299344a8efb2fdff8daa4 <http://schema.org/value> "Blyth" .
_:b25ebb43d837adbdbd136ad0c43a9fd <http://schema.org/value> "Blyth Offshore Demonstrator Ltd/EDF Renewables" .
_:ce70941e050299344a8efb2fdff8daa4 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8acd87656971ac7295a4a18820c2732a4e8b633d> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b25ebb43d837adbdbd136ad0c43a9fd .
_:edd8da592c4d2fa94a414718c5617fe7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:edd8da592c4d2fa94a414718c5617fe7 <http://schema.org/value> "multibeam bathymetry" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8acd87656971ac7295a4a18820c2732a4e8b633d> <http://schema.org/description> "Bibby HydroMap were commissioned by Blyth Offshore Demonstrator Ltd/EDF Renewables, in August 2018, to undertake a series of geophysical surveys at the Blyth Offshore Demonstrator wind farm, located off the north-east coast of the UK at Blyth, Northumberland. \r\n The 41.5 MW wind farm is located approximately 6km offshore of Blyth and comprises five wind turbine generators configured in a single row, as indicated in Figure 1 below. Surveys have been previously undertaken in August/September 2018, April 2019, and this, the most recent survey, was undertaken between the 29th October and 20th November 2019.\r\n Due to the general lack of seabed mobility, the survey boundary for this monitoring visit has been reduced to decrease survey acquisition and processing timescales for the client. The new boundaries were submitted to and approved by the Marine Management Organisation (MMO) in October 2019.\r\nThis survey, comprising the collection of multibeam bathymetry and side scan sonar data, marks the third of a 3-year monitoring program, which will be undertaken at 6 monthly intervals, and after any major storm events. \r\nThe objectives of the survey program were to acquire survey data to a resolution that will:\r\nIdentify seabed debris within the construction area; \r\n- Identify changes to seabed morphology to enable the evaluation of the effectiveness of installed scour protection and ratify predictions for scour development; \r\n- Inform the foundation and cable maintenance schedule; \r\n- Satisfy the requirements of the Marine Licence." .
_:edd8da592c4d2fa94a414718c5617fe7 <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
