_:e65030014fee8a86ebfebfe2d00cf744 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:88e78f92a74f8a973bab32031f566bf178fce456> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:88e78f92a74f8a973bab32031f566bf178fce456> <http://schema.org/description> "This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. \r\n This feature class records the number of individuals involved in general scuba diving and snorkelling on a monthly basis. The month fields record the number of interviewees that have contributed to this data, the fields with a count suffix record the number of individuals. Individual records have been summarised onto a grid 3/4 nautical mile longitude by 3/8 nautical mile latitude.\r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:88e78f92a74f8a973bab32031f566bf178fce456> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e65030014fee8a86ebfebfe2d00cf744 .
_:d7b9faf19baeb9a70f8b9ba00e026259 <http://schema.org/value> "GEO" .
_:fb4571aa758da67145398477de772873 <http://schema.org/value> "Sufford Coast" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:88e4700e197b013eb2814a786fb758d6f4037a68> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:a473c07ee108fcd601d08c6776726927 <http://schema.org/value> "sleeve friction" .
_:d7b9faf19baeb9a70f8b9ba00e026259 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:a473c07ee108fcd601d08c6776726927 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
_:fb4571aa758da67145398477de772873 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:a473c07ee108fcd601d08c6776726927 <http://schema.org/value> "pore\r\npressure effects" .
_:a473c07ee108fcd601d08c6776726927 <http://schema.org/value> "cone resistance" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:88e4700e197b013eb2814a786fb758d6f4037a68> <http://schema.org/description> "Greater Gabbard Offshore Winds Ltd. (GGOWL) has contracted Noordhoek Offshore B.V. with\r\nGEO (Danish Geotechnical Institute) as sub-contractor to conduct geotechnical work in terms\r\nof seabed CPT’s (Cone Penetration Test) for The Greater Gabbard Offshore Wind Farm Project.\r\nTest site is located approximately 26 km (14 nautical miles) off the Sufford Coast at Felixstowe/\r\nHollesley Bay.\r\nThe geotechnical work has including seabed CPTs at the planned wind park turbine locations\r\nand at a part of the Cable Route Corridors. Totally 138 CPTs have been carried out for the\r\nwind turbines and 9 CPTs for the cable routes.\r\nThis report presents the results from these investigations. The report includes factual data\r\nincluding both measured cone resistance and sleeve friction and values corrected for pore\r\npressure effects. No interpretations of the measured data are included in this report." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:88e4700e197b013eb2814a786fb758d6f4037a68> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fb4571aa758da67145398477de772873 .
