<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:82216eab46c2dbff1c4f595bab128c8e8521ed9d> <http://schema.org/description> "Data provided by the Environment Agency to ISCZ for identification of MCZs.\r\n European Eel are listed as a Species feature of conservation importance (Highly Mobile) and are also Listed as Critically Endangered on the IUCN Red List a\r\n UKBAP Priority Species and a species of principal importance for the purpose of conserving of biodiversity under the Natural Environment and Rural Communities Act 2006\r\n \r\n JNCC and Natural England are licensed to use this data untill 17/11/2011" .
_:bf545adb3bb2cbc603969df0e53077f9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:be8328d11a919121f43b826c9794bc86 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:82189d32514a2c78da9d01b015853824b7e83c41> <http://schema.org/description> "Survey run by Ambios Environmental Consultants Ltd. for Kerr-McGee Oil (UK) plc. All these records relate to \"Cleator (1995) - Lyme Bay Environmental Study Volume 3. Subtidal benthic ecology: Epibenthos\" A copy of the report is held at Dorset Environmental Records Centre.\r\n This report forms part of the 'Lyme Bay Environmental Study' series. This volume investigates the hard substratum communities in the eastern section of Lyme Bay (Lyme Regis to Portland Bill). The use of SCUBA was restricted to areas shallower than 30m and involved the survey of 13 sites. Dives were conducted between 29th June - 13th July 1994. The survey was undertaken from the MV Sea Urchin. The location of each site was determined using Differential Global Positioning System. An additional 29 sites were surveyed using an ROV in areas not covered by the diving survey - these are covered in an appendix to this report." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:82189d32514a2c78da9d01b015853824b7e83c41> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:da98277c796396cc7ce960df7368cfb3 .
