_:a9a033fd944ea74d6848a793b2be43a5 <http://schema.org/value> "Irish Sea" .
_:c8bea251d71252def5f7fd370e7e3357 <http://schema.org/value> "Celtic Sea" .
_:c8bea251d71252def5f7fd370e7e3357 <http://schema.org/value> "Clyde Sea" .
_:c8bea251d71252def5f7fd370e7e3357 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:81ecadb17c4bb6943a91ad13751875035b05b275> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset comprises hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, during April - May 1981. It incorporates a CTD grid survey of the Irish Sea. The data were collected by the University of Wales, Bangor School of Ocean Sciences as part of a survey cruise contributing to research directed toward understanding how the physics of the Irish Sea and surrounding regions (Celtic Sea, St, George's Channel, North Channel and Clyde Sea) determine biogeochemical processes and sediment transport." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:81ecadb17c4bb6943a91ad13751875035b05b275> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:a9a033fd944ea74d6848a793b2be43a5 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:c8bea251d71252def5f7fd370e7e3357 <http://schema.org/value> "North Channel" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:81ecadb17c4bb6943a91ad13751875035b05b275> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c8bea251d71252def5f7fd370e7e3357 .
_:a9a033fd944ea74d6848a793b2be43a5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d9c7e02afd01982c95fe3df98cbe0892 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:d9c7e02afd01982c95fe3df98cbe0892 <http://schema.org/value> "CT Offshore" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:81e309ed63f06f1061ef855e2980273145ae720f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d9c7e02afd01982c95fe3df98cbe0892 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:81e309ed63f06f1061ef855e2980273145ae720f> <http://schema.org/description> "The export of power from the WODS offshore wind farm is transferred through 2 designated main export power\r\ncables connecting the wind farm with onshore installations.\r\nThe scope of work carried out by CT Offshore has been to complete a MBES, SSS and a TSS rov survey of both\r\ncables, from here and onwards designated as the northern and southern WODS export cable.\r\nThe task and objective of the MBES and SSS is to identify and report abnormalities such as exposed cables and\r\ninterfering object along and in relation to the cable position and map the seabed bathymetry as well." .
_:d9c7e02afd01982c95fe3df98cbe0892 <http://schema.org/value> "SSS" .
_:d9c7e02afd01982c95fe3df98cbe0892 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:81e309ed63f06f1061ef855e2980273145ae720f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:da130bcf5c6c4abc85b1f0f673919ee3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:da130bcf5c6c4abc85b1f0f673919ee3 <http://schema.org/value> "Centre for Environment, Fisheries and Aquaculture Science" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:81db97a04158f18c37528a95e6d3784d4cd69794> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:da130bcf5c6c4abc85b1f0f673919ee3 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:81db97a04158f18c37528a95e6d3784d4cd69794> <http://schema.org/description> "Full coverage multibeam survey collecting bathymetry and backscatter to client specifications, namely International Hydrographic Organization (IHO) Order 1a standard, WGS84 latitude and longitude co-ordinates collected by Differential Global Positioning System (DGPS), depths corrected to Chart Datum (CD). Main survey lines run at 125m spacing with crosslines every 7km. Raw and processed data delivered to Centre for Environment, Fisheries and Aquaculture Science, UK (Cefas) complete with georeferenced mosaics and GeoTiffs images. These data are archived with the Marine Environmental Data and Information Network (MEDIN) Data Archive Centres (DACs) including the British Geological Survey (BGS) DAC for geology and geophysics, The Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data (DASSH) and the United Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO) bathymetry DAC. The full site data package including raw is also available on request from BGS." .
_:da130bcf5c6c4abc85b1f0f673919ee3 <http://schema.org/value> "Marine Environmental Data and Information Network" .
_:da130bcf5c6c4abc85b1f0f673919ee3 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:da130bcf5c6c4abc85b1f0f673919ee3 <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey" .
_:da130bcf5c6c4abc85b1f0f673919ee3 <http://schema.org/value> "United Kingdom Hydrographic Office" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:81db97a04158f18c37528a95e6d3784d4cd69794> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:da130bcf5c6c4abc85b1f0f673919ee3 <http://schema.org/value> "Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data" .
