<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d77db69d2d512652c64aa8eb178aeee140b24ae> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d77db69d2d512652c64aa8eb178aeee140b24ae> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bd08d12238427bbe28e2427317d9971a .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d77db69d2d512652c64aa8eb178aeee140b24ae> <http://schema.org/description> "This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. \r\n This feature class records the number of vessels carrying survey teams on a month by month basis. Individual records have been summarised onto a grid 3/4 nautical mile longitude by 3/8 nautical mile latitude.\r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record." .
_:bd08d12238427bbe28e2427317d9971a <http://schema.org/value> "Stakmap/Fishermap" .
_:bd08d12238427bbe28e2427317d9971a <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
_:bd08d12238427bbe28e2427317d9971a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d49ba5d112f4b167d1d1e305edf6e500fc2d4e2> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:da63ec06a81dc62a63d5c7b1271bff78 .
_:da63ec06a81dc62a63d5c7b1271bff78 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d49ba5d112f4b167d1d1e305edf6e500fc2d4e2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:da63ec06a81dc62a63d5c7b1271bff78 <http://schema.org/value> "HR Wallingford" .
_:da63ec06a81dc62a63d5c7b1271bff78 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d49ba5d112f4b167d1d1e305edf6e500fc2d4e2> <http://schema.org/description> "This study follows on from two previous metocean studies carried out in 2004 and 2008 by HR Wallingford for the Lynn and Inner Dowsing Offshore Wind Farm, and for the Lincs Wind Farm.\r\n\r\nA SWAN spectral wave model was set up in 2007 by HR Wallingfor to supply operational forecasts of nearshore waves at the Lynn and Inner Dowsing wind farm. This is a more sophisticated model that the HINDWAVE/TELURAY wave model used in HR Wallingford (2004). This SWAN model was calibrated against various measurements in the Lincs wind farm study (HR Walligford, 2008) and provides an accurate description of the waves across the area of the wind farms. A Telemac 2D flow model was also set up and calibrated against various measurements during the Lincs Wind Farm study.\r\n\r\nIn this study, the updated and improved wave and flow conditions were extracted from teh models calibrated in the Lincs study area (HR Wallingford, 2008) in the four nearshore points defined in the previous HR Wallingford report." .
_:d9c77a96f5d1a35bbb6bc4ee25cf69c3 <http://schema.org/name> "taxon" .
