<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:77f4e322d536de46ddb0ae7b1260a5754904bbbc> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d2d73d70b944f4815e8632904f4d3f2a .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:77f4e322d536de46ddb0ae7b1260a5754904bbbc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:d2d73d70b944f4815e8632904f4d3f2a <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:77f4e322d536de46ddb0ae7b1260a5754904bbbc> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d29b0480e080c6eb2bfea315ab0e546b .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:77f4e322d536de46ddb0ae7b1260a5754904bbbc> <http://schema.org/description> "Spectrum Geosurvey Limited was contracted by London Array Limited (hereinafter ‘the Client’)\r\nto survey six pre-defined corridors across the London Array Offshore Windfarm site including\r\nsubstations 1 and 2.\r\nThe surveys were performed on board the survey / crew transfer vessel Spectrum 1. The primary\r\nobjective was to collect high resolution multibeam bathymetry and backscatter data over the\r\ndefined survey areas. This data was required to provide a comparison with previous datasets and\r\nto assess any changes in seabed level and morphology." .
_:d2d73d70b944f4815e8632904f4d3f2a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c791d093e5b48ec37479a860c33a6927 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
