_:f007884a5af2ef2a56bb977eee72b928 <http://schema.org/value> "Cornwall Council" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:72aca7179c56707085966035519e03f1cacb7a49> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f007884a5af2ef2a56bb977eee72b928 .
_:f007884a5af2ef2a56bb977eee72b928 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:72aca7179c56707085966035519e03f1cacb7a49> <http://schema.org/description> "In March 2009 English Heritage commissioned Historic Environment Projects, Cornwall Council to carry out an initial theoretical study to result in an Updated Project Design (UPD) to inform field trials of different types of marine magnetometer in controlled conditions. The project was funded through the Aggregates Levy Sustainability Fund (ALSF). The main part of the theoretical study was carried out by a team of external maritime and/or geophysics specialists." .
_:fe44bc4812dd4fc8dfce89e0e925f149 <http://schema.org/value> "Kongsberg Maritime Ltd" .
_:fe44bc4812dd4fc8dfce89e0e925f149 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:cfbc2a93d677951f02edc744ef3a609f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:72aaa53b8087c56e825dd8910c78a33952758a86> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fe44bc4812dd4fc8dfce89e0e925f149 .
_:fe44bc4812dd4fc8dfce89e0e925f149 <http://schema.org/value> "Marine Current Turbines Ltd" .
_:d96669bdc81eae9fce524ac7e8dc44dd <http://schema.org/value> "weighted\r\nmeasurements by M" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:72aaa53b8087c56e825dd8910c78a33952758a86> <http://schema.org/description> "This document has been prepared by Kongsberg Maritime Ltd\r\nfor Marine Current Turbines Ltd, of Bristol, England. The report\r\ndescribes field measurement methods, data processing and\r\npresentation, of underwater sound attributed to the operation of\r\nthe SeaGen electrical power generator.\r\nSound recordings in the vicinity of the unit were made over a\r\nperiod of 2 days, at various states of tide, with the unit running\r\nand idle.\r\nThe sound recordings were made using a high fidelity digital\r\nsystem, and all data stored for post processing. The recorded\r\ndata includes time and position stamping.\r\nThe sound data has been post processed to provide intensity vs\r\nrange plots, with Power Spectral Densities and weighted\r\nmeasurements by M, and dBht factors appropriate to the local\r\nmammalian fauna.\r\nThe measured sets are presented as colour graduated charts of\r\nthe SeaGen location." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:72aaa53b8087c56e825dd8910c78a33952758a86> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d96669bdc81eae9fce524ac7e8dc44dd .
