<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6e7dff1b6a9685baab454d0f1bc504ba1aff3bb0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:d43e74c4d2f2d772942dfaf9ce0d810d <http://schema.org/value> "Osiris Projects" .
_:d43e74c4d2f2d772942dfaf9ce0d810d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6e7dff1b6a9685baab454d0f1bc504ba1aff3bb0> <http://schema.org/description> "Osiris Projects were commissioned by E.ON Climate &amp; Renewables UK to carry out a\r\ndetailed hydrographic and geophysical survey for the Humber Gateway ‘Round Two’\r\noffshore wind farm development area and its associated export cable routes.\r\nSurvey data were acquired across the footprint of the main development site and the\r\ntwo, 1km-wide export cable route corridors (indicated below), the survey extents of\r\nwhich were provided by the Client.\r\naddition, survey data were also acquired at a number of 100m x 100m boxes, which\r\nwere centrally positioned at proposed borehole locations and orientated NNW to SSE\r\nto minimise the effects of any tidal currents on line keeping.\r\nThese additional boxes were undertaken to provide information as to potential UXO\r\nrisk to Contractors and for jack-up rig leg penetration/support calculations." .
_:d43e74c4d2f2d772942dfaf9ce0d810d <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
_:d73aca6567e24257ed3060409079cca0 <http://schema.org/value> "hydrographic data profiles" .
_:d73aca6567e24257ed3060409079cca0 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6e62a635c5d190676d65b97d686ea60866d6599f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:dc3889857a58e829dee311d7746675f8 .
