_:c006f5f04c98921129051a6daa4b7291 <http://schema.org/value> "npower renewables" .
_:d068a16f0ef3ff2f2053430a92585958 <http://schema.org/value> "Triton Knoll" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6d704f8f193cbe7aa2a3cd3aeda4aaa95af6c57e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:d068a16f0ef3ff2f2053430a92585958 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d068a16f0ef3ff2f2053430a92585958 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:c006f5f04c98921129051a6daa4b7291 <http://schema.org/value> "Emu Ltd" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6d704f8f193cbe7aa2a3cd3aeda4aaa95af6c57e> <http://schema.org/description> "In December 2003, npower renewables (NR) was granted a Round II wind farm exploration licence by the\r\nCrown Estate in an area known as Triton Knoll. In April 2004, NR commissioned Emu Ltd to undertake a\r\nGIS-based review of the constraints in relation to the Triton Knoll site. This review concluded that due to\r\nthe number of potential constraints associated with the original Triton Knoll site, there may be potentially\r\nmore suitable areas within the Greater Wash Strategic Environmental Assessment (SEA) area for\r\ndevelopment. Consequently, Emu Ltd was requested to review constraints within the entire SEA area and\r\nidentify any potential areas for development. Following this wider review, 4 additional potential\r\ndevelopment areas were identified (Area 1 - Holderness, Area 2 - Modified Triton Knoll, Area 3 - Dudgeon\r\nShoal and Area 4 - Sole Pit/Well Hole)." .
_:c006f5f04c98921129051a6daa4b7291 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6d6e5de7448c2433a2569c3e6c643ddee739f7f1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a11d7045dc1611fc2699cb149b95cf16 .
