_:d2910f4af56fa9ad6be2fb5b5738d017 <http://schema.org/value> "Wessex Archaeology" .
_:d2910f4af56fa9ad6be2fb5b5738d017 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6d6bf1b882f941cd549c413f4cb9b7bd85abf36a> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d7fe33f42a415b75a98ba02ea04a8ece .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6d6bf1b882f941cd549c413f4cb9b7bd85abf36a> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology was commissioned by English Heritage to carry out an archaeological assessment of previously uninterpreted geophysical data acquired from an area of the East Goodwin Sands. Analysis of the data has revealed a total of 256 anomalies of archaeological potential from within the Study Area, including five potential wreck sites, six potential dispersed wreck sites and a potential cannon site." .
_:d7fe33f42a415b75a98ba02ea04a8ece <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:f149616d4cbe81ebf03d865a08ea1415 <http://schema.org/value> "Iberian Peninsula" .
