_:b64a9f2f2c8105eb8e6a2f6bbc6f4275 <http://schema.org/value> "Eddystone Plymouth" .
_:a9e8b3552d32f64ee574e145cef3e04d <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
_:e10dfaa746aea64503375ebece4aca0b <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:621b6cce1eca0dd967a6ab8ad14d489d46c3fcf4> <http://schema.org/description> "Ad-hoc series of events carried out in the Gara point, Stoke point, Plymouth Sound and Plymouth Sound Approaches area in 2007 using SeaSearch methodology. Data on species and biotope recorded and entered onto Marine Recorder. Species data and biotope data mapped as points using MapInfo. Includes the 2007 Seasearch survey of Gara point to Stoke point, 2007 Seasearch survey of Plymouth Sound, 2007 Seasearch survey of Plymouth Sound Approaches, and the 2007 Seasearch survey of The Eddystone Plymouth." .
_:b64a9f2f2c8105eb8e6a2f6bbc6f4275 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:e10dfaa746aea64503375ebece4aca0b <http://schema.org/name> "taxon" .
_:b64a9f2f2c8105eb8e6a2f6bbc6f4275 <http://schema.org/value> "Gara point" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:621b6cce1eca0dd967a6ab8ad14d489d46c3fcf4> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e10dfaa746aea64503375ebece4aca0b .
_:b64a9f2f2c8105eb8e6a2f6bbc6f4275 <http://schema.org/value> "Stoke point" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:621b6cce1eca0dd967a6ab8ad14d489d46c3fcf4> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b64a9f2f2c8105eb8e6a2f6bbc6f4275 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:621b6cce1eca0dd967a6ab8ad14d489d46c3fcf4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:61ee51e4afa75817347e6c51bdef8308496b6db1> <http://schema.org/description> "This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. \r\n \r\n This feature class records the number of people involved in bird watching, mammal watching or botany. Total number of people per annum is recorded by the GroupN field the count field records the number of interviews that contributed to this data.\r\n Individual records have been summarised onto a grid 3/4 nautical mile longitude by 3/8 nautical mile latitude.\r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record." .
_:e4c7dba0e0ba720d10625ae6725b7b81 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e4c7dba0e0ba720d10625ae6725b7b81 <http://schema.org/value> "Stakmap/Fishermap" .
_:e4c7dba0e0ba720d10625ae6725b7b81 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
