<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:56643c77b9ea14e34d7c99d2ee67637a35576c92> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:cce3c3b895824d00c6c9f112f446992d .
_:cce3c3b895824d00c6c9f112f446992d <http://schema.org/value> "Osiris Projects Ltd" .
_:cce3c3b895824d00c6c9f112f446992d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:56643c77b9ea14e34d7c99d2ee67637a35576c92> <http://schema.org/description> "As part of the site development at Gunfleet Sands, a detailed geophysical survey was conducted from\r\nSeptember to December 2006 by Osiris Projects Ltd to establish subsurface conditions prior to piling and ploughing operations. The survey was designed specifically to provide very accurate bathymetry data and a high-resolution magnetic data set that would prove to be a valuable tool in the detection of maritime\r\narchaeological features and unexploded ordnance. For more information about Analysis of ROV Targets from April / May 2007 by RPS Hydrosearch, please see the \"Gunfleet Sands Analysis of ROV Targets\" project." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:56643c77b9ea14e34d7c99d2ee67637a35576c92> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bbabbb1d58686aa9847161b4d6b9927f .
_:cce3c3b895824d00c6c9f112f446992d <http://schema.org/value> "RPS Hydrosearch" .
_:cce3c3b895824d00c6c9f112f446992d <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:bbabbb1d58686aa9847161b4d6b9927f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c08f23c985b0d8830968ef4ccf26354a <http://schema.org/value> "bathymetry data" .
_:bbabbb1d58686aa9847161b4d6b9927f <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:565e5f6a6fb3235e809d00b4f43ee3703e7a7ab7> <http://schema.org/description> "Four 0.01m2 cores were taken at each site. The survey was carried out in November 1991 by the NRA South West Region. Samples were also taken for particle size analysis and organic carbon/nitrogen analysis. Data on species and biotope recorded and entered onto Marine Recorder. Species data and biotope data mapped as points using MapInfo." .
