<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:521aae39f03e03775ab51eea956c8479f84ca1b7> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d46638a72e9e40b0294b2d22d15ed6ad .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:521aae39f03e03775ab51eea956c8479f84ca1b7> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fa9f746e1e019e78009836c25810a34f .
_:fa9f746e1e019e78009836c25810a34f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:521aae39f03e03775ab51eea956c8479f84ca1b7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:521aae39f03e03775ab51eea956c8479f84ca1b7> <http://schema.org/description> "On the instructions of RSKENSR Environment Limited, Osiris Projects were commissioned to carry out a Post Construction Geophysical Survey covering \r\n the existing Barrow Offshore Wind Farm development. The Scour Monitoring Survey was undertaken in conjunction with the Post Construction Geophysical Survey, meaning \r\n all equipment on board the vessel was utilised along all survey lines. This included high-resolution swathe multi-beam, side scan sonar and single beam\r\n bathymetry data. A total of 288km of geophysical data were collected during the post-construction geophysical survey, whilst a total of 12.15km of \r\n geophysical data were collected for the scour monitoring survey, which was curtailed due to continuing poor weather. Data acquisition took place during\r\n the period 25th September to 3rd November 2006, with survey works undertaken using the survey vessel MV ‘Freja’." .
_:d46638a72e9e40b0294b2d22d15ed6ad <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
