_:d524c4f18d4cdf57d2c0369486684702 <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51ee279ea894ba5c19b2025e920adec8b0e119ad> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d524c4f18d4cdf57d2c0369486684702 .
_:d524c4f18d4cdf57d2c0369486684702 <http://schema.org/value> "boat surveys" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51ee279ea894ba5c19b2025e920adec8b0e119ad> <http://schema.org/description> "Between December 2003 and November 2004, defined as Year 3 of this study, a total of seventeen boat surveys of birds and marine mammals were carried out around the Kentish Flats Wind Farm site. Approximately one third of these covered the wind farm site, the buffer and the control area, whilst the remainder covered only the wind farm site and the buffer. Additionally three aerial surveys were carried out in Year 3 over a wider area extending beyond the wind farm site, and another aerial survey was undertaken on 5 December 2004. The February survey took place over three days, though all of the wind farm, buffer zone and control areas were covered on 15 February 2004. Previously, between October 2001 and November 2003 (Years 1 and 2) forty boat surveys of birds and marine mammals had been carried out around the Kentish Flats Wind farm site. Over these earlier periods a total of five aerial surveys were carried out over a wider area extending beyond the wind farm site. This Monitoring report in this series analyses the results of the 12 months of boat data collected from December 2003 to November 2004 for the Kentish Flats wind farm project, and aerial data collected over that period at the wind farm site and the surrounding area." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51ee279ea894ba5c19b2025e920adec8b0e119ad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:b5ca364e168a9ae051a73d85e052e7be <http://schema.org/value> "Kentish Flats Wind farm site" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51ee279ea894ba5c19b2025e920adec8b0e119ad> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b5ca364e168a9ae051a73d85e052e7be .
_:a066bceba4a5e5b61531d75557127287 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51e4a8c5f16821251fb8e95e4ab86b4dce0d3728> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51e4a8c5f16821251fb8e95e4ab86b4dce0d3728> <http://schema.org/description> "This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. \r\n This feature class records the number of individuals watching wildlife or engaged in botany It describes these values on a month by month basis. The month fields record the number of interviewees that have contributed to this data, the fields with a count suffix record the number of individuals. Individual records have been summarised onto a grid 3/4 nautical mile longitude by 3/8 nautical mile latitude.\r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51e4a8c5f16821251fb8e95e4ab86b4dce0d3728> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a066bceba4a5e5b61531d75557127287 .
_:a066bceba4a5e5b61531d75557127287 <http://schema.org/value> "Stakmap/Fishermap" .
_:a066bceba4a5e5b61531d75557127287 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51e234f821e563d3464d843e4a9da02e9d5da9e4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:c4fe4f9b3c03cd846496da5326a255a7 <http://schema.org/value> "Dudgeon Offshore Wind Limited" .
_:c4fe4f9b3c03cd846496da5326a255a7 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51e234f821e563d3464d843e4a9da02e9d5da9e4> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c4fe4f9b3c03cd846496da5326a255a7 .
_:c4fe4f9b3c03cd846496da5326a255a7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51e234f821e563d3464d843e4a9da02e9d5da9e4> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology was commissioned by Dudgeon Offshore Wind Limited to prepare an archaeological desk based and geophysical assessment for the offshore elements of the Dudgeon Offshore Wind Farm project including the export cable route and landfall. The Offshore Wind Farm Study Area measured approximately 66 km2, the export cable route measured approximately 36 km in length, and the terrestrial Study Area comprised a 1 km buffer at the cable terminus. This assessment informed the Environmental Statement. The known archaeology consisted of: 12 wrecks and obstructions; 243 geophysical anomalies; and 133 terrestrial find spots, sites and archaeological activities. The potential archaeology consists of 31 documented losses; unknown and undocumented shipwrecks from various periods; stray finds of ship borne debris from various periods; potential for the presence of submerged palaeo-landscapes, dating from 700,000 BP to the Romano-British period; and potential for unknown terrestrial material from the Palaeolithic to present." .
_:b3f1676a1a30119adc450107c8764840 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51d0a698d20060b2d35bdbfe6aeb781d0258c227> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:51d0a698d20060b2d35bdbfe6aeb781d0258c227> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 2 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from the East Atlantic area specifically just North of the McGowan Seamount and the Kane Gap, East of Guinea, from January to April 1968. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the National Institute of Oceanography." .
_:a0b13db93f1dd20a6c7f1a3490852d32 <http://schema.org/value> "Kane Gap" .
