_:dd5753fb9744617353e048e8ed8fe9b6 <http://schema.org/value> "sidescan sonar" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4ff350cbd7c3b7c639c57536f2dc587640c8315e> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ca0a769e74a78eb0645f0524bf818ca4 .
_:dd5753fb9744617353e048e8ed8fe9b6 <http://schema.org/value> "grab sampling survey" .
_:d87e25767732e3932fca5073dfc9f700 <http://schema.org/value> "United Marine Dredging" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4ff350cbd7c3b7c639c57536f2dc587640c8315e> <http://schema.org/description> "Geophysical and Geotechnical survey of a 7.2km area located between and partly within dredging areas 197 and 106 (licensed to United Marine Dredging, and Hanson Aggregates Marine Ltd, respectively). The area lies some 16km east of Donna Nook, Lincolnshire.The survey was commissionned by English Heritage and funded through Round 2 of the Aggregate Levy Sustainability Fund (ALSF), and was part of the wider ALSF 'Seabed Prehistory' project. The survey comprised bathymetric survey, sidescan sonar, and shallow seismic survey. A grab sampling survey was also undertaken, and a series of vibrocores were taken to calibrate the geophysical data. (Study area coords: E332472, N5921678; E333629, N5921945; E335016, N5916074; E333793, N5915802 - WGS84, UTM zone 31). OSL and radiocarbon dating of deposits from vibrocores, dates sediments in the North Sea at 20m below OD to the late Mesolithic period." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4ff350cbd7c3b7c639c57536f2dc587640c8315e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
