<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:44b171964026fbdc82bc9681940c35adcc15dbd6> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f8d971f0efac42b27521347bc43060c2 .
_:d95e9334e7e10dfab24b48acf1892fdc <http://schema.org/value> "Water Depths" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:44b171964026fbdc82bc9681940c35adcc15dbd6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:44b171964026fbdc82bc9681940c35adcc15dbd6> <http://schema.org/description> "A geological model is developed for the Burbo Bank wind farm site which is located approximately 25km north-west of LIverpool, in the south-eastern Irish Sea. Water Depths range from approximately 5m to 28m and are at their shallowest where sand banks occur. This study integrates available geophysical (sparker and pinger) data, with geotechnical data, including vibrocores (GEO, 2012) and boreholes (FESL, 2013)." .
_:bb50015046b12150c96373e6fb3a824a <http://schema.org/value> "Irish Sea" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4495a103a92dc48e1a9e0e0f83fa6efb5dfb9138> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c508575f146765e79419e8448f5a2c94 .
_:c508575f146765e79419e8448f5a2c94 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:eeed1038602795e87c955eed67a76f60 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4495a103a92dc48e1a9e0e0f83fa6efb5dfb9138> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4495a103a92dc48e1a9e0e0f83fa6efb5dfb9138> <http://schema.org/description> "ABP Marine Environmental Research Ltd (ABPmer) has been commissioned by \r\nDONG Energy Power (DONG) to undertake a metocean study for the proposed \r\nWestermost Rough Offshore Wind Farm. The proposed development site is within the \r\nGreater Wash area, established from the Strategic Environmental Assessment (SEA) \r\nfor Round 2 offshore wind farms (BMT Cordah, 2003). More specifically, the site is \r\nlocated, approximately, 8km off the Holderness Coast with a development area of \r\n35km2, providing the potential for up to 240MW of installed capacity with between 60 to \r\n80 turbines. The project site has a relatively uniform seabed profile ranging in depth \r\nfrom around 11m to more than 20m Chart Datum (CD), and is devoid of any major \r\nsandbank features. \r\nThe report within this series presents the study findings, which are presented according to the study \r\nspecification." .
_:c508575f146765e79419e8448f5a2c94 <http://schema.org/value> "DONG Energy Power" .
_:b0aadf245bc4833aa2e275b338d8b060 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
