_:b11f9bfd3d960344a7cb33ad593d5c86 <http://schema.org/value> "Celtic Array" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:40b588bc428692a4f1fa61602c46e5301f21ea53> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b11f9bfd3d960344a7cb33ad593d5c86 .
_:a97f5a6d55ce757b92227748a694d0c5 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:a97f5a6d55ce757b92227748a694d0c5 <http://schema.org/value> "Stanah" .
_:b11f9bfd3d960344a7cb33ad593d5c86 <http://schema.org/value> "Renewable Energy Systems Ltd" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:40b588bc428692a4f1fa61602c46e5301f21ea53> <http://schema.org/description> "Celtic Array commissioned Renewable Energy Systems Ltd (RES) in 2011 to carry out a desk review of potential landfall locations around the north coast of Anglesey and Stanah for Round 3 Irish Sea Zone grid connection[1]. From this review, 25 potential landfall locations were identified on Anglesey and of these 24 locations, 11 of the landfall locations were identified as providing the most promising solutions for a grid connection on Anglesey. A series of site visits were conducted March 2011 to verify the engineering suitability of the 11 selected landfall locations and to support the recommendations made.\r\n\r\nCorresponding Centrica Document No: R3-D-GC-001-0000-000000-005\r\n\r\nAvailable dataset : Reports in pdf formats, GIS data in MXD, shapefile format," .
_:e6bd76ca7f6ce13164b165cf1f857daa <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:40ac3d0311c82e76504819c22e774dfdc5408470> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e9c4e3ebed3d8ccaf57936b270bb406f .
_:fd5f87daa1ec46e3c37f42bbc6142e59 <http://schema.org/value> "Unexploded Ordnance Survey" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:40ac3d0311c82e76504819c22e774dfdc5408470> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e6bd76ca7f6ce13164b165cf1f857daa .
_:e9c4e3ebed3d8ccaf57936b270bb406f <http://schema.org/value> "Wessex Archaeology" .
_:e6bd76ca7f6ce13164b165cf1f857daa <http://schema.org/value> "Protection of Military Remains Act 1986" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:40ac3d0311c82e76504819c22e774dfdc5408470> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fd5f87daa1ec46e3c37f42bbc6142e59 .
_:fd5f87daa1ec46e3c37f42bbc6142e59 <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
_:e9c4e3ebed3d8ccaf57936b270bb406f <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:fd5f87daa1ec46e3c37f42bbc6142e59 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e9c4e3ebed3d8ccaf57936b270bb406f <http://schema.org/value> "Galloper Wind Farm Limited" .
_:e9c4e3ebed3d8ccaf57936b270bb406f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:40ac3d0311c82e76504819c22e774dfdc5408470> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:e9c4e3ebed3d8ccaf57936b270bb406f <http://schema.org/value> "Ministry of Defence" .
_:fd5f87daa1ec46e3c37f42bbc6142e59 <http://schema.org/value> "remotely operated vehicle (ROV) survey" .
_:e6bd76ca7f6ce13164b165cf1f857daa <http://schema.org/name> "policies" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:40ac3d0311c82e76504819c22e774dfdc5408470> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology was commissioned by Galloper Wind Farm Limited to undertake a review of an area of archaeological material identified during Unexploded Ordnance Survey of the Offshore Wind Farm, undertaken as part of the Galloper Offshore Wind Farm project. Wessex Archaeology's assessment of remotely operated vehicle (ROV) survey data interpreted it as debris from an aircraft crash site dating to the Second World War, comprising a concentration of aluminium sheets, other aluminium material, wires, metal debris, possible canvas fabric and lightweight fabric. A temporary Archaeological Exclusion Zone (AEZ) was initially recommended, however, as the proposed locations of the array cables would impact the area, and following consultation with Historic England, the temporary AEZ was removed, and further discussions regarding mitigation for the site were initiated. The Protection of Military Remains Act 1986 applies to the fabric and contents of the aircraft - including cargo and crew. Given the identification of the site as likely Second World War military aircraft material, the Ministry of Defence has been consulted. Intentional disturbance of the site without a licence or permission would be in breach of the Act." .
_:b5fe459ac973764231dccb2eca6bef6d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:40a9d166e16753145282c78ad5175f1567d232dd> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b5fe459ac973764231dccb2eca6bef6d .
