<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:36c7656426e1cd02422d7d0fc908a480f865e8f8> <http://schema.org/description> "Benthic monitoring of the sea bed adjacent to the fish farm as a requirement of the CAR licence for the site. Grab samples collected in proximity to the farm and at two reference locations. Samples analysed for: benthos, redox, psa, carbon and sea louse medicine residues." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:36beb77adc4d0da5d6bb2ff0dae4e35ebd0318dc> <http://schema.org/description> "Osiris Projects were commissioned in January 2015 by DONG Energy to carry out a geophysical and\r\nUXO survey at the planned Burbo Bank extension Offshore Windfarm site. The survey was completed\r\nunder Osiris Projects Terms and Conditions. The main site survey, the northern section of the export\r\nroute and Option 1 environmental survey were carried out\r\nbetween 16th February 2015 and 11th April 2015 on board the MV Bibby Tethra.\r\nFollowing demobilisation of SV Bibby Tethra on the 11th April 2015 a small number of bathymetric and\r\nmagnetometer infills were identified during processing. These infill lines were completed by MV\r\nProteus and MV Chartwell, which were on site working on the southern sections of the export route.\r\nMV Proteus mobilised for the job on the 22nd-24th April 2015, and demobilised on 27th June 2015. MV\r\nChartwell mobilised for the job on the 18th and 19th of May 2015, demobilising on the 5th June 2015.\r\nThe main objectives of the survey were to provide:\r\n1. High resolution bathymetry. \r\n2. Geomorphologic features on the seabed\r\n3. Identification and quantification of possible biogenic reefs." .
