_:b32d2ec911c24966206132b47b6610f5 <http://schema.org/value> "abundance" .
_:b32d2ec911c24966206132b47b6610f5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3460cff0825998a28aa703b51c7a9f65c1eea12f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b32d2ec911c24966206132b47b6610f5 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3460cff0825998a28aa703b51c7a9f65c1eea12f> <http://schema.org/description> "Ornithological boat-based surveys have been conducted to inform of any changes to the abundance and\r\ndistribution of species between the pre-construction and during-construction periods of the Lincs/LID6 Wind\r\nFarm. This interim report presents the results of the surveys during the period August to October 2012,\r\nwhich formed part of the Year 2 Construction period.\r\nIn general, estimated numbers in 2012 were largely similar to those found in previous years within this\r\nperiod, and where there were some differences (e.g. Sandwich tern, razorbill), it could not be determined\r\nwith any confidence that this was due to the presence of Lincs/LID6 construction activities or part of a wider\r\nnatural variation in numbers. There was however no clear evidence that any key species have been\r\nadversely affected by such construction activities. This information will form part of a more comprehensive\r\nYear 2 Construction period annual report, which will statistically test for any changes in the abundance and\r\ndistribution of species in relation to the Lincs/LID6 construction activities." .
_:b32d2ec911c24966206132b47b6610f5 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3460cff0825998a28aa703b51c7a9f65c1eea12f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f8fbdc8e3fc7077e5758bd29c31dd4ab .
_:f8fbdc8e3fc7077e5758bd29c31dd4ab <http://schema.org/value> "Sandwich tern" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3460cff0825998a28aa703b51c7a9f65c1eea12f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:f8fbdc8e3fc7077e5758bd29c31dd4ab <http://schema.org/value> "razorbill" .
_:f8fbdc8e3fc7077e5758bd29c31dd4ab <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d5d19c827ab8937c7727b00f8f5bcd8a <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:d5d19c827ab8937c7727b00f8f5bcd8a <http://schema.org/value> "AIS" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34360acf7708af68c748f9e58e1f6de2b1caff23> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d5d19c827ab8937c7727b00f8f5bcd8a .
_:d5d19c827ab8937c7727b00f8f5bcd8a <http://schema.org/value> "Anatec" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34360acf7708af68c748f9e58e1f6de2b1caff23> <http://schema.org/description> "Anatec were commissioned by Centrica Renewable Energy Ltd to assess the risk of damage to their planned cable route in The Wash from vessels dragging anchor and from emergency anchoring. This report presents an update to the risk assessment, using 12 months of AIS data collected from September 2011 to August 2012.\r\nThis report summarises the data sources, methodology and results. The results are presented in terms of the annual frequency of an anchor dragging over the cable or a vessel dropping anchor on the cable; and the frequency of cable damage, based on the as-laid burial depth of the cable and the estimated anchor penetration depth." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34360acf7708af68c748f9e58e1f6de2b1caff23> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:d5d19c827ab8937c7727b00f8f5bcd8a <http://schema.org/value> "Centrica Renewable Energy Ltd" .
_:d5d19c827ab8937c7727b00f8f5bcd8a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ca3f35e17d80a01281671e315353337a <http://schema.org/value> "Fisheries Mapping Project" .
_:abdc319ab6bf105fadc3d87c6dc125f5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34214bd242e149d14bcef3797bb8874c03893f6f> <http://schema.org/description> "This layer is the output of the Eastern Sea Fisheries Joint Committee's Fisheries Mapping Project, which aimed to describe-using best available data and fishermens knowledge-the extent of the main fisheries within the ESFJC District.\r\n \r\n They are not, however, exhaustive-please use with discretion. Use of this data should never replace full, proper consultation within the fishing industry, but rather be seen as illustrative of the types of activity within the District and, where information is available, an indication of seasonality. \r\n A report on the Fisheries Mapping Project will be available in Spring 2012, and will contain information about how the data was collected and compiled, and the process of consultation which was undertaken. Please refer to the ESFJC website: www.eastern-ifca.gov.uk\r\n \r\n For further details on the project, its output, or guidance on how to interpret the data, please contact the project manager: jwoo@esfjc.co.uk.\r\n \r\n To register for updates to these layers (including forthcoming addition of metadata), please register your interest at jwoo@esfjc.co.uk. \r\n \r\n (Please acknowledge use of Fisheries Mapping Project data. It can be cited as: ESFJC, 2010- ESFJC District Fisheries Mapping Project)." .
_:ca3f35e17d80a01281671e315353337a <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34214bd242e149d14bcef3797bb8874c03893f6f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:ca3f35e17d80a01281671e315353337a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
