<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:312a66530a8949456d6866e721720f00eef147f2> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c71dd1dababb5d1cbe886ff8fe3f8349 .
_:e275e9f9ccb216e401cdb0a14a35f13a <http://schema.org/value> "WTGs LS28" .
_:c01c14a122231719935c2d136e63fe37 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:311e6e25fd1a06c451b8963989647604de4e85b5> <http://schema.org/description> "After completion of the depth of burial survey of the Lincs Array Cables project, and the Export Cablesurvey, EGS (International) Ltd, on behalf of Centrica, undertook a Side-Scan Sonar (SSS) and Multibeam (MBES) clearance survey of the no cable zones (500m by 500m) around WTGs LS28 (on the Lincs site) and ID24 (on the Inner Dowsing site). The areas surveyed were identified by Centrica for the upcoming works on the aforementioned turbines and the need to get a jack up vessel in the locality to complete the works. This report details the operations and results of the survey around ID24. \r\n\r\nPort Sutton Bridge was used as the base port of operations for the survey. Mobilisation was carried out in conjunction with the Export Cable survey and was completed on the 4th June 2014. The survey operations took place on the 6th and 7th of June 2014. Demobilisation commenced on the 7th June and was completed on the 8th June 2014. This work was carried out by EGS on behalf of Centrica and this report covers TURBINE ID24 CLEARANCE SURVEY" .
_:c01c14a122231719935c2d136e63fe37 <http://schema.org/value> "depth" .
