_:c412814ce5232929fb85bb91ad5093d1 <http://schema.org/value> "Withernsea" .
_:bae40b724d2b86d661d7ab99f7d4e422 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:30c1f4c4a476da1457619538e449f64727266dbc> <http://schema.org/description> "Part of the larger 'England's Historic Seascapes' project, funded through the Aggregate Levy Sustainability Fund (ALSF) and distributed by English Heritage (EH). This part of the project characterised the historic coastal, inter-tidal and marine zone 'land'scapes between Withernsea and Skegness in the East Ridings of Yorkshire, extending out to the medial line with Holland. The characterisation is intented to inform both coastal and marine management and planning. Site coordinates given are for Withernsea and Skegness. Full study area (which includes 120km of the tidal Humber estuary) is shown in project report. Maximum depth is estimated from the approximate Marine limit of the study area, as it relates to SeaZone Hydrospatial depth data, height above OD is not known. Neither limit is specified in the project report. More details about the project are available on the Archaeology Data Service website - http://archaeologydataservice.ac.uk" .
_:a65bbad5752ab052b711234e45f7cc92 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:30a1a9f77c973e62e135d86289be066f8f28b127> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset comprises hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, in March 1985. It incorporates a survey of the North Channel between Scotland and Northern Ireland. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Food Lowestoft Fisheries Laboratory." .
_:a65bbad5752ab052b711234e45f7cc92 <http://schema.org/value> "Scotland" .
_:a65bbad5752ab052b711234e45f7cc92 <http://schema.org/value> "North Channel" .
_:a65bbad5752ab052b711234e45f7cc92 <http://schema.org/value> "Northern Ireland" .
_:a65bbad5752ab052b711234e45f7cc92 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:30a1a9f77c973e62e135d86289be066f8f28b127> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a65bbad5752ab052b711234e45f7cc92 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:30a1a9f77c973e62e135d86289be066f8f28b127> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:a70816bbb5cc2975e9b1eb7d0d394b90 <http://schema.org/value> "North Channel" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:30a02e83b74edb85bf03f3eba222a5cda48b0941> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 73 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the Irish Sea and surrounding regions (Celtic Sea, St. George's Channel, North Channel and Clyde Sea) during the month of May in 1985. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the University of Wales, Bangor School of Ocean Sciences." .
_:f86cd657fe85093a71dbe650ad4f9928 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
