<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2bdf607c3667b444008d8bf797442a405ab636d3> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d7dff7063ba9a90cc46faf51ce1e805c .
_:b71de79f0d9ea8734512a0ddf7be0d83 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2bcf4a9dd3ae70eecd572df00e4180a7f67ce7fb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2bcf4a9dd3ae70eecd572df00e4180a7f67ce7fb> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b71de79f0d9ea8734512a0ddf7be0d83 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2bcf4a9dd3ae70eecd572df00e4180a7f67ce7fb> <http://schema.org/description> "Geotechnical investigation to provide sufficient data to enable the zone-wide characterisation of the soil and rock conditions for combination with the regional geophysical data to inform the technical and commercial planning process. This investigation was for the Centrica round 3 Irish Sea - Zone 9 Offshore Wind Farm Development. It was carried out by Fugro Geoconsulting Limited using the vessel: MV Normand Mermaid Corresponding Centrica Document No: SE-D-EN-127-0117-501003-005 Available Datasets and supporting documentation: 1.AGS data (.ags) 2.Wireline Digital Data (.las, .xls) 3. Images(.pdf, jpg)" .
_:b71de79f0d9ea8734512a0ddf7be0d83 <http://schema.org/value> "Fugro Geoconsulting Limited" .
_:b71de79f0d9ea8734512a0ddf7be0d83 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:d8444e51f83050aa667d39f382aaa928 <http://schema.org/value> "MARICO Marine" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2bc75de39d990b8f665216c5568623a713fba3d5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:d8444e51f83050aa667d39f382aaa928 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2bc75de39d990b8f665216c5568623a713fba3d5> <http://schema.org/description> "MARICO Marine was commissioned by Greater Gabbard Offshore Winds Limited to conduct a maritime traffic survey on and around the area of the proposed Greater Gabbard Offshore Wind Farm located approximately 20 miles East of Harwich. The survey covered a total period of 24 days, seven days during the summer and seventeen days during the winter months of 2004 and provides a record of all vessel tracks through the area allowing identification of shipping routes. \r\n\r\nAnatec UK Ltd used the data collected by MARICO Marine to carry out a shipping assessment. The study analyses the traffic survey data collected by MARICO Marine and assesses the risk of ships on the two main routes encountering / colliding with the proposed wind farm structures.\r\n\r\nSeaRoc UK Ltd used the data collected by MARICO Marine to carry out a Navigational Risk Assessment of the site of the proposed Greater Gabbard offshore wind farm." .
_:d8444e51f83050aa667d39f382aaa928 <http://schema.org/value> "Anatec UK Ltd" .
