_:ae6345ce8912bcd1f19cdc5e59c496dc <http://schema.org/value> "Colonsay" .
_:da557f7d01a0fc739879410082f69cdc <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey (BGS)" .
_:ae6345ce8912bcd1f19cdc5e59c496dc <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:23222379c625c6e189313a3cfe1c07d8cce255fc> <http://schema.org/description> "This marine sampling survey took place in August 2015 in the area of Firth of Lorne and east of Colonsay on board the NLV Pharos. The survey was carried out by the British Geological Survey (BGS). The aim of the survey was to test the BGS seabed rockdrill RD2. These data are archived by BGS." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2321fe3bb6ad583302b45391a77380486069d362> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e8226847a3653b98651e151bace2b637 .
_:e8226847a3653b98651e151bace2b637 <http://schema.org/value> "North East Atlantic Ocean" .
_:bed996dfb0f4c4dd4a87e9d2dbcf068a <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2321fe3bb6ad583302b45391a77380486069d362> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset comprises hydrographic data profiles, collected by a salinity-temperature-depth (STD) sensor package, during September 1978. It incorporates STD casts performed within the North East Atlantic Ocean area, incorporating parts of the Rockall via Anton Dohrn (Ellett Line) section and triangular surveys around each of the Joint Air Sea Interaction Experiment (JASIN) moorings NW of the Anton Dohrn Seamount. The data were collected by the Scottish Marine Biological Association." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2321fe3bb6ad583302b45391a77380486069d362> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bed996dfb0f4c4dd4a87e9d2dbcf068a .
_:e8226847a3653b98651e151bace2b637 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:bed996dfb0f4c4dd4a87e9d2dbcf068a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e8226847a3653b98651e151bace2b637 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:bed996dfb0f4c4dd4a87e9d2dbcf068a <http://schema.org/value> "Scottish Marine Biological Association" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2321fe3bb6ad583302b45391a77380486069d362> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2315af7dc6bd834026f46ff21b71d6e6e11fa840> <http://schema.org/description> "Natural Resources Wales (NRW), Natural England (NE) and the Joint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC) have produced advice documents providing an overview of the ecological sensitivities to marine aggregate extraction within Welsh and English inshore and offshore waters. These documents contain detail on the pressures and environmental impacts associated with aggregate dredging, including the habitats, species and marine protected areas most sensitive to these impacts. \r\n The aim of these documents is to help inform prospective lease applicants in the siting of potential marine aggregate extraction activities as part of The Crown Estateâ??s 2021/22 aggregates licensing round. \r\n These documents were produced for The Crown Estate. The advice provided is not exhaustive and does not replace the need for a detailed assessment of individual projects. It is therefore non-binding and provided without prejudice to any further advice given or decisions made by NRW, NE and the JNCC. It is recommended that operators engage with the relevant statutory nature conservation body as early as possible when planning marine aggregate extraction to avoid significant environmental and consenting risks." .
_:e05ac95dec59c5d99a6cf0276fa7ffc6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d67c3885f82f1ba0a7078c55c55f59dc <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
