<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2266f007120f4e2dda0d33b75fc3856f2e6fcef1> <http://schema.org/description> "Osiris Projects were commissioned in August 2012 by SSE Renewables, Costa Head Wave Farm Ltd and Brims Tidal Array Ltd to carry out three contractually separate geophysical surveys around Orkney, at Costa Head, Westray South and Brims, to assess the suitability of the locations for the potential installation of wave / tidal generators, beginning with the associated cable routes. Initial surveys were undertaken with MV Lia between 17th August and 3rd October 2012, and with MV Chartwell between 22nd August and 18th September 2012. The surveys were not completed by this date and the project was, therefore, suspended for the winter period. Osiris Projects were re-commissioned in March 2013 and the surveys continued with MV Bibby Tethra between 12th April and 19th May 2013, and with MV Lia between 19th May and 28th September 2013, whereupon the three survey areas were deemed complete." .
_:f90e018bf91f21ad502dc55ecaeb0a9a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
