<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:13fd62b32aae1705b2a262ee999a1789be58d5bb> <http://schema.org/description> "This report covers an Undesignated Site Assessment of the possible wreck site of UB-31, lost off Folkestone on 2nd May 1918. The work was carried out as part of the Heritage at Risk (HAR) contract for archaeological services in relation to marine designation. Wessex Archaeology carried out this project, which was commissioned before English Heritage and Historic England became two separate organisations. Thus where English Heritage is referenced in the report, these functions have been transferred to Historic England." .
