<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:07d0541e9378585c13ae6b9d0aa5a22327343cff> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a6f9da9d4451422f3ed8212c25c13a5f .
_:d372550cc932ffedf77d681a98498e85 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:079977e565366e7d87137fb29fa33bc33967f07f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:079977e565366e7d87137fb29fa33bc33967f07f> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset represents a snapshot of MPA search location boundaries as of the Fifth Workshop (http://www.scotland.gov.uk/Topics/marine/marine-environment/mpanetwork/engagement/270612) which was held on the 27 and 28 June 2012 to present progress on the emerging shape of the proposed MPA network. Search location profiles for Existing (http://www.scotland.gov.uk/Topics/marine/marine-environment/mpanetwork/engagement/140312/locations) and Additional (http://www.scotland.gov.uk/Topics/marine/marine-environment/mpanetwork/engagement/140312/additional) MPA search locations at Workshop 4, as well as Third Party Proposals (http://www.scotland.gov.uk/Topics/marine/marine-environment/mpanetwork/engagement/140312/thirdparty), can still be viewed to illustrate the evolution of the boundaries during the process when compared to the NMPi map." .
_:d372550cc932ffedf77d681a98498e85 <http://schema.org/value> "locations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:079977e565366e7d87137fb29fa33bc33967f07f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d372550cc932ffedf77d681a98498e85 .
